mber/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:15:01-07:00","id":1063561,"title":"","content":"Focused Mastigos Sight, activate! Form of: Scanner!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:16:36-07:00","id":1063562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063558#post1063558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Divination returns an error. You don't know what that means. You didn't even know error was an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Postcognition near an Iris? Does it show Jim getting inside?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:19:37-07:00","id":1063565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063561#post1063561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Focused Mastigos Sight, activate! Form of: Scanner!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Iris resonates most strongly with Space and what you believe to be Prime symbolism. While you can generally see hints of the other arcana there, these are the two that resonate most strongly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:20:53-07:00","id":1063567,"title":"","content":"Any more detail on the Prime symbolism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:25:06-07:00","id":1063572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063562#post1063562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Postcognition near an Iris? Does it show Jim getting inside?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? It is somewhat strange. He doesn't so much <i>enter</i> the Iris. That would imply movement. It was more like one moment he was standing before it, something magical happened, probably it opening, and the next instant he was gone. You <i>think</i> he went in, but looking back through postcognition, you can't really find <i>when</i>. One instant he was outside, the next, presumably inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:27:25-07:00","id":1063574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063572#post1063572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe? It is somewhat strange. He doesn't so much <i>enter</i> the Iris. That would imply movement. It was more like one moment he was standing before it, something magical happened, probably it opening, and the next instant he was gone. You <i>think</i> he went in, but looking back through postcognition, you can't really find <i>when</i>. One instant he was outside, the next, presumably inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so we need to check his Mind via Mind Sight via Postcognition. As I asked - is there a way to grant it to my cabalmates? Maybe they can look it up in my head while I use Postcognition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:27:50-07:00","id":1063575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063567#post1063567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any more detail on the Prime symbolism?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, you aren't that familiar with Prime, though you've dabbled in it enough to get something. They're like strange Prime veiling symbols. You think they might be there to hide the Iris from magic or something but it isn't really doing that good of a job at it so you aren't sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063574#post1063574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so we need to check his Mind via Mind Sight via Postcognition. As I asked - is there a way to grant it to my cabalmates? Maybe they can look it up in my head while I use Postcognition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I'd let you do it for a reach, and since we aren't really rolling, go for it. Your cabal mates can see what you can now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-16-2017, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:33:45-07:00","id":1063582,"title":"","content":"Okay, I kinda lost track of that we are doing here. This isn't really a murder case by anyone (or it is really strange one; I don't think anybody would create a Time-distorting Iris just for killing one mage) and Postcognition isn't working on exact moment of death (not for Time magic interruption, but nonetheless), so it isn't what I was talking about. What's the point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:34:19-07:00","id":1063583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063574#post1063574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I asked - is there a way to grant it to my cabalmates? Maybe they can look it up in my head while I use Postcognition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scale would be the way to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:37:41-07:00","id":1063588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063582#post1063582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I kinda lost track of that we are doing here. This isn't really a murder case by anyone (or it is really strange one; I don't think anybody would create a Time-distorting Iris just for killing one mage) and Postcognition isn't working on exact moment of death (not for Time magic interruption, but nonetheless), so it isn't what I was talking about. What's the point?</div> </div> </div> </div>One, I never said what was going on was simple. Two, I never said anyone died (yet, because as far as you know, no one has died yet), and the point is showing you that a mystery is usually not as simple as it seems. You went in with the assumption that lol murder mysteries are easy, but nothing is easy when mages are involved, not good ones anyways. Now then, how about we solve this mystery? =3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063583#post1063583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scale would be the way to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you are correct! Forgot about scale for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:42:59-07:00","id":1063590,"title":"","content":"I keep at scrutiny, hoping to get at Deep Information, saying aloud whatever i find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:43:56-07:00","id":1063591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063583#post1063583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scale would be the way to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes. Thanks, I forgot about one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063588#post1063588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the point is showing you that a mystery is usually not as simple as it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first, I wasn't saying anything about Mysteries. Only murders by mages. Second, you made it not as simple by saying &quot;lol, Postcognition won't work&quot;. Sure thing everytask become a lot less simple if you take away main instrument of mage. That isn't really demonstrating what I was saying, unless every murder in your game includes rules-breaking Irises in unknown locations.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:49:13-07:00","id":1063593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063590#post1063590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep at scrutiny, hoping to get at Deep Information, saying aloud whatever i find.</div> </div> </div> </div>After several minutes of intense scrutiny, you are fairly confident that wherever this leads isn't normal. You've heard rumors of strange places, like verges and the strange places they lead to. The Supernal, the Shadow, places wholly lacking in some fundamental part of reality, and stranger things still. This could lead to any one of those. The fact of the matter is, you simply aren't familiar enough with these places to identify which.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:50:05-07:00","id":1063594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063572#post1063572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe? It is somewhat strange. He doesn't so much <i>enter</i> the Iris. That would imply movement. It was more like one moment he was standing before it, something magical happened, probably it opening, and the next instant he was gone. You <i>think</i> he went in, but looking back through postcognition, you can't really find <i>when</i>. One instant he was outside, the next, presumably inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the Iris formed on top of him? Did it exist before he disappeared there since you can use mage sight through postcognition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:50:15-07:00","id":1063595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063591#post1063591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yes. Thanks, I forgot about one.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, first, I wasn't saying anything about Mysteries. Only murders by mages. Second, you made it not as simple by saying &quot;lol, Postcognition won't work&quot;. Sure thing everytask become a lot less simple if you take away main instrument of mage.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A murder by a Mage using Magic = A Mystery<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063591#post1063591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That isn't really demonstrating what I was saying, unless every murder in your game includes rules-breaking Irises in unknown locations.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>OK, you use Postcognition on Jim from a few hours ago. You see him at home and then he bursts into flame and is reduced to dust ashes in seconds. Now what do you do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Fixing quote block 03-16-2017, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:56:02-07:00","id":1063600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063595#post1063595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, you use Postcognition on Jim from a few hours ago. You see him at home and then he bursts into flame and is reduced to dust ashes in seconds. Now what do you do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Use Postcognition to Mage Sight the spell which was used. Try to understand who could use such spell and which Yantra he used for Sympathetic Range. Check Sympathetic connections formed at the moment and after the death, try to find new receptor of them. Maybe use Temporal Summoning for checking location for Signature Nimbus. Combining Time and Space may be able to check past sympathetic connections. And so on.<br /> Also, get other mages to work on this murder. Maybe this spontaneous combustion is \u0441ontagious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 03-16-2017, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:59:55-07:00","id":1063603,"title":"","content":"(this thread is going to make me such a better Mage ST, I swear)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:00:31-07:00","id":1063604,"title":"","content":"At this point it can be completely within the rules, aThysus with Mind could have compelled Jim to Spirit verge and use the key that the Thyrsus knew, and had his spirit ally to devour Jim alive, leaving only Spirit ephermera as evidence in the hisil (because you're transmuted into ephemera when you pass through the verge)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:00:54-07:00","id":1063605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063591#post1063591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yes. Thanks, I forgot about one.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, first, I wasn't saying anything about Mysteries. Only murders by mages. Second, you made it not as simple by saying &quot;lol, Postcognition won't work&quot;. Sure thing everytask become a lot less simple if you take away main instrument of mage. That isn't really demonstrating what I was saying, unless every murder in your game includes rules-breaking Irises in unknown locations.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Murders by Mages <i>are</i> Mysteries. This might seem shocking, but sometimes, in a story, things don't work. I'm giving you a realistic example of how a story might progress. Though if you really want it to be played straight, then you all were mind controlled a few minutes into the adventure. And yes, you're going to bring up how you checked to see if you were going to be attacked, and the answer was no when you checked, but I said that when it was just you and the alchemist. You brought the hacker into the equation. You changed the base situation and never checked to see if in doing so you changed what happens.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I could have made it simple, but simple wouldn't have been as interesting, because simple, assuming I was playing it straight with an opponent who honestly wanted you dead would be over really quickly. Now I could have just gone with Prime and had the theoretical killer shield himself against magical scans and searches while doing the deed but then this really would have gotten nowhere, because postcognition still wouldn't have worked and you'd still be mad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063594#post1063594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like the Iris formed on top of him? Did it exist before he disappeared there since you can use mage sight through postcognition?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kinda like standing on a contact portal that opens for a split second. You get dragged in and then it instantly closes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063604#post1063604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point it can be completely within the rules, aThysus with Mind could have compelled Jim to Spirit verge and use the key that the Thyrsus knew, and had his spirit ally to devour Jim alive, leaving only Spirit ephermera as evidence in the hisil (because you're transmuted into ephemera when you pass through the verge)</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my lower key explanation, but I wanted something a bit more mysterious, so I decided on something else pretty quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-16-2017, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:03:05-07:00","id":1063606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063600#post1063600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Use Postcognition to Mage Sight the spell which was used. Try to understand who could use such spell and which Yantra he used for Sympathetic Range. Check Sympathetic connections formed at the moment and after the death, try to find new receptor of them. Maybe use Temporal Summoning for checking location for Signature Nimbus. Combining Time and Space may be able to check past sympathetic connections. And so on.<br /> Also, get other mages to work on this murder. Maybe this spontaneous combustion is \u0441ontagious.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You get a sense of Spirit but its not Supernal Magic.<br /> <br /> Shortuct: Because I don't have the time that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2309\" data-vbnamecard=\"2309\">Ashenrogue</a> does to go through a whole game (which I love by the way). It was a Thyrsus who used a Fire Spirit to do it. Now you have to try and track down a Spirit, the trail leads into the Shadow... Adventure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:03:21-07:00","id":1063607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063603#post1063603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(this thread is going to make me such a better Mage ST, I swear)</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to get something out of this too. For example, an interesting MO for mage-killers like Banishers and Scelesti for players to discover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:04:03-07:00","id":1063608,"title":"","content":"What I don't understand is that when you're presented with a mystery that doesn't involve just walking up to a person and murdering them in the face you have a ready list of steps you'd take, and because you can think of a method of investigation this somehow makes murder mysteries too easy to solve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:09:28-07:00","id":1063613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063607#post1063607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to get something out of this too. For example, an interesting MO for mage-killers like Banishers and Scelesti for players to discover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, are we going to finish it? Standing around doesn't seem to be getting you anywhere. You could go in and continue the adventure or leave and wait for other consilium mages to do it for you.<br /> <br /> What do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-16-2017, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:09:31-07:00","id":1063614,"title":"","content":"Here's one: You use PostCognition on Jim and you see <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12981_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12981\" data-vbnamecard=\"12981\">RomulusGloriosus</a> 's character walk up to him all friendly and then suddenly stab him with a large knife and then slit is throat. They clean the knife and then calmly walk away. What do you do?<br /> <br /> \u200bInspired by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> ' post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Added some attribution. 03-16-2017, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:12:55-07:00","id":1063616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063593#post1063593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After several minutes of intense scrutiny, you are fairly confident that wherever this leads isn't normal. You've heard rumors of strange places, like verges and the strange places they lead to. The Supernal, the Shadow, places wholly lacking in some fundamental part of reality, and stranger things still. This could lead to any one of those. The fact of the matter is, you simply aren't familiar enough with these places to identify which.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cursing under my breath, i think for a second. I go to the abandonned car and search it for emotionally-resonant and -fresh items, paying attention to the steering wheel, pedals and gear-shift to get a feel for Jim's emotional state and reasoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:13:18-07:00","id":1063617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063605#post1063605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Murders by Mages <i>are</i> Mysteries. This might seem shocking, but sometimes, in a story, things don't work. I'm giving you a realistic example of how a story might progress.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063605#post1063605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, you're going to bring up how you checked to see if you were going to be attacked, and the answer was no when you checked, but I said that when it was just you and the alchemist. You brought the hacker into the equation. You changed the base situation and never checked to see if in doing so you changed what happens.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b I also constantly check the future for signs of trouble. </div> </div> </div>You know what &quot;constantly&quot; means, right? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063605#post1063605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah, I could have made it simple, but simple wouldn't have been as interesting, because simple, assuming I was playing it straight with an opponent who honestly wanted you dead would be over really quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so, without overwhelming advantage in firepower? Surprise doesn't really means anything, if both sides know about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063605#post1063605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I could have just gone with Prime and had the theoretical kill shield himself against magical scans and searches while doing the deed but then this really would have gotten nowhere, because postcognition still wouldn't have worked and you'd still be mad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could've burned through by repeated attempts or bringing up stronger mages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:14:02-07:00","id":1063618,"title":"","content":"This thread is why you want a cabal that has at least two members covering at least every Arcana, and barring that being a member of an Assembly or Colesium that has an investigation team that does...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:14:04-07:00","id":1063619,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2309\" data-vbnamecard=\"2309\">Ashenrogue</a> I thought you were gonna somehow bring the Seers into it, since you set up the whole thing at the beginning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:17:00-07:00","id":1063621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063618#post1063618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is why you want a cabal that has at least two members covering at least every Arcana, and barring that being a member of an Assembly or Colesium that has an investigation team that does...</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is, if you're too spread out as a cabal, you lose out on team spellcasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:18:04-07:00","id":1063622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063613#post1063613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, are we going to finish it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, it's too late in my timezone and this argument won't bring us anywhere, sadly. I'm out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:21:20-07:00","id":1063627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063617#post1063617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You know what &quot;constantly&quot; means, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> How so, without overwhelming advantage in firepower? Surprise doesn't really means anything, if both sides know about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Could've burned through by repeated attempts or bringing up stronger mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't catch constant, but honestly, with the way time magic works I could easily make it the last time you check that they attack. You'd get hit literally as soon as went to cast, since that would have been the one to change things.<br /> <br /> Because mages play rocket tag. It really isn't that hard for one mage to kill another, and you had absolutely nothing up to stop soooo many forms of instagibbing you.<br /> <br /> And those mages would have turned you down because you had no proof of anything and they'd be wasting their time. Other mages aren't there to do your work for you. At least at my table, if you don't have some heavy proof of immediate concern, while they might help you eventually, it won't be a priority.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063619#post1063619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2309\" data-vbnamecard=\"2309\">Ashenrogue</a> I thought you were gonna somehow bring the Seers into it, since you set up the whole thing at the beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of those things that I would have likely brought up in a future session after you think you were going to have some downtime. More of a 'and now, after overcoming the trials set before you, you are finally allowed to rest. Or so you thought...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063616#post1063616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cursing under my breath, i think for a second. I go to the abandonned car and search it for emotionally-resonant and -fresh items, paying attention to the steering wheel, pedals and gear-shift to get a feel for Jim's emotional state and reasoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>You pick up a lot of old, familiar resonance from the car, calm, anger, happiness, things you're used to. Jims had the car for awhile so all of this is generally what you would expect to find. However, the 'freshest' resonance is that of barely contained, giddy excitement. Whatever it was, it seemed like Jim was really looking forward to it. It could have been his thoughts of hanging out at the bar with you guys, but you can't really imagine he'd be that excitement about something so mundane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-16-2017, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:32:15-07:00","id":1063634,"title":"","content":"Here's another thing about mysteries, typically people (Mages included) don't bother to look beyond the most obvious answer. We like to apply Occam's Razor. Adding even one layer of complexity to a mystery can be enough to throw off an investigation. This happens with regrettable frequency in law enforcement. For instance there was a case of a professor at a college who was murdered in her classroom in a brief period between classes. A homeless man who liked to hang out on campus was convicted for the crime due to enough circumstantial evidence. Decades later video footage came to light -that the prosecution had- of him sleeping on a bench that was time stamped for the time during which the murder had to have occurred. The prosecution had this conflicting piece of evidence, but since it didn't fit their preconception of the case or some of the other evidence they pushed for and got the conviction of an innocent man. There's probably some systemic problems going on there, but it's unlikely the prosecution intended to convict an innocent man, they just decided to ignore the video evidence that conflicted with their preconceptions. Mages are powerful, but just as prone to these kinds of human mistakes. Now, in a game, eventually, all is supposed to come to light, but a smart ST can toy with their players' preconceptions and mislead them quite easily for as long as the story requires without the need for &quot;Your powers don't work here.&quot; or other gimmicks. (Though a good gimmick can also be fun once in a while!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:42:12-07:00","id":1063642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063627#post1063627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of those things that I would have likely brought up in a future session after you think you were going to have some downtime. More of a 'and now, after overcoming the trials set before you, you are finally allowed to rest. Or so you thought...<br /> <br /> <br /> You pick up a lot of old, familiar resonance from the car, calm, anger, happiness, things you're used to. Jims had the car for awhile so all of this is generally what you would expect to find However, the 'freshest' resonance is that of barely contained, giddy excitement. Whatever it was, it seemed like Jim was really looking forward to it. It could have been his thoughts of hanging out at the bar with you guys, but you can't really imagine he'd be that excitement about something so mundane.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take something of his - his keys probably - in case I'll need it. I walk up to the iris and cast Outward and Inward eye with the +2 Reach effect to try and see though it. I use the keys (iron wands?) to build my imago around looking through keyholes. (Net 3 reach, 2 of which are free)<br /> <br /> (Although if it has prime it probably won't work)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 03-16-2017, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:48:28-07:00","id":1063647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063622#post1063622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, it's too late in my timezone and this argument won't bring us anywhere, sadly. I'm out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you're that put off by an actual game-type example, then a simpler example of a less capable mage would be something like Mind 2, Space 3, Prime 2. Indefinite Cloak Nimbus and Supernal Veil, then sympathetically using Psychic Domination on someone and commanding them to kill people. Even easier if the person dominated is a part of a preexisting crime ring. Hell, they could probably just Psychic Dominate the mage victim in question and have them kill themselves. There's pretty much no way to track them down for a single murder. It would take crazy intense investigation trying to find the link between multiple murders. You could probably do about the same substituting Mind for spirit and having a spirit do it. Or Fate. Or Death. Or just about anything really","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:52:31-07:00","id":1063651,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Spirit/Ghost assassins are brutally effective, and disposable. Even just stabbing someone from twilight using Reaching is really friggin effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:54:23-07:00","id":1063653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063642#post1063642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I take something of his - his keys probably - in case I'll need it. I walk up to the iris and cast Outward and Inward eye with the +2 Reach effect to try and see though it. I use the keys (iron wands?) to build my imago around looking through keyholes. (Net 3 reach, 2 of which are free)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's relatively dark, that's the first thing you notice. The second is that the walls seemed to be made of damp, uneven stone. A cave perhaps? The only light to speak of is cast by a line of faintly burning torches; Seemingly spaced quit a bit apart giving the dreariness of the scene before you. The path stretched forward, curving downwards, deeper into what you assume to be the earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T17:06:26-07:00","id":1063658,"title":"","content":"Not. good.<br /> Also i just realized that Correspondence can reveal keys. I use Correspondence at +2 reach and +1 potency to know what the key is.<br /> (I'm still not used to the new edition's spells)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T17:17:02-07:00","id":1063669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063658#post1063658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not. good.<br /> Also i just realized that Correspondence can reveal keys. I use Correspondence at +2 reach and +1 potency to know what the key is.<br /> (I'm still not used to the new edition's spells)</div> </div> </div> </div>Any spell incorporating those specific Prime symbols observed when examining the Iris can act as the Key. You believe that Romulus might be able to do so. They seemed fairly simple, and he at least knows the basics of Prime spells. In fact, they seem so simple that with his help, you might be able to incorporate them into an imago of your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-16-2017, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T18:58:45-07:00","id":1063705,"title":"","content":"Can I be one of the characters? This plot is so cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T19:08:57-07:00","id":1063709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063705#post1063705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I be one of the characters? This plot is so cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately we've seen to have wound down. I fear progressing much further would risk straying into Off Topic territory since Dark Archon doesn't really except the example I was trying to set, which was the entire point. That and I'm not sure if this is even the appropriate section for this kinda thing. I mean I don't think it was strictly against the rules, but I get the feeling that running a straight up chronicle might belong somewhere else (I'd have to check).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T19:23:21-07:00","id":1063714,"title":"","content":"Aaah. T-T<br /> <br /> Well, just to explain the things I would try to use:<br /> <br /> Acanthus Mystagogue (Time 3, Fate 2, Death 1, Life 1)<br /> <br /> I would have used Exceptional Luck to give me Charmed Condition (For defensive purposes, so any damage would be reduced to 1).<br /> <br /> Then I would cast Divination with reach(For more specific answers) and ask for these 3 questions:<br /> 1. Will I found my cabalmate still alive in the near future?<br /> 2. Am I mortally endagering myself with this search?<br /> 3. Any other members of my cabal will be endangered by following this trail?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> Back on topic. I also think that this example and some others that I'm thinking really explain the fact that Time magic isn't perfect for finding Assassin Mages. It certainly helps, but it's not the ultimate Arcana to do this. And it needs a damn whole lot of legwork and solving the pieces of the puzzle, without getting murdered/captured/soulstealed doing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 03-16-2017, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T20:39:21-07:00","id":1063737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063634#post1063634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another thing about mysteries, typically people (Mages included) don't bother to look beyond the most obvious answer. We like to apply Occam's Razor. Adding even one layer of complexity to a mystery can be enough to throw off an investigation. This happens with regrettable frequency in law enforcement. For instance there was a case of a professor at a college who was murdered in her classroom in a brief period between classes. A homeless man who liked to hang out on campus was convicted for the crime due to enough circumstantial evidence. Decades later video footage came to light -that the prosecution had- of him sleeping on a bench that was time stamped for the time during which the murder had to have occurred. The prosecution had this conflicting piece of evidence, but since it didn't fit their preconception of the case or some of the other evidence they pushed for and got the conviction of an innocent man. There's probably some systemic problems going on there, but it's unlikely the prosecution intended to convict an innocent man, they just decided to ignore the video evidence that conflicted with their preconceptions. Mages are powerful, but just as prone to these kinds of human mistakes. Now, in a game, eventually, all is supposed to come to light, but a smart ST can toy with their players' preconceptions and mislead them quite easily for as long as the story requires without the need for &quot;Your powers don't work here.&quot; or other gimmicks. (Though a good gimmick can also be fun once in a while!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you mind giving an example for this? Because while the example of the murder with the video is realistic it wouldnt fly with players. Players see such a absolute evidence and they immediately fly into &quot;he is innocent&quot;. While real people in the real world can and do ignore the absolute truth in favor of their pre-conconceptions, a player that shoot themselves on the leg to that level is rare and not a measuring stick by any means.<br /> <br /> As for this thread original question, lower case mysteries arent a story you can really tell in mage unless either<br /> <br /> A) You go full plot convenience as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2309\" data-vbnamecard=\"2309\">Ashenrogue</a> went and put high concept things like Irises.<br /> <br /> B) Nerf mages.<br /> <br /> And to be fair thats something that happens in many games, some splat you make difficult of impossible to tell certain kinds of stories with a certain focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 03-16-2017, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T21:46:05-07:00","id":1063745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063737#post1063737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you mind giving an example for this? Because while the example of the murder with the video is realistic it wouldnt fly with players. Players see such a absolute evidence and they immediately fly into &quot;he is innocent&quot;. While real people in the real world can and do ignore the absolute truth in favor of their pre-conconceptions, a player that shoot themselves on the leg to that level is rare and not a measuring stick by any means.<br /> <br /> As for this thread original question, lower case mysteries arent a story you can really tell in mage unless either<br /> <br /> <b>A) You go full plot convenience as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2309\" data-vbnamecard=\"2309\">Ashenrogue</a> went and put high concept things like Irises.</b><br /> <br /> B) Nerf mages.<br /> <br /> And to be fair thats something that happens in many games, some splat you make difficult of impossible to tell certain kinds of stories with a certain focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, at least going by the what we were talking about in the thread you can totally do lower case m mysteries involving other mages. I just chose not to because Archon seemed like he would have taken anything simple other than absolute shutdown (which is boring) as a sign that Time alone was impossible to get around. Instead, I constructed a situation in which things weren't as simple as they appeared going into it that, while solvable, wasn't something looking back in time would solve in and of itself.<br /> <br /> Assuming you are in a normal game where you can freely allow characters the option of figuring things out using their preferred method you can much more easily use lesser methods without being forced to make it nigh-impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-17-2017, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T23:00:18-07:00","id":1063750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063709#post1063709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the feeling that running a straight up chronicle might belong somewhere else (I'd have to check).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Play By Post subforum in the Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play board where people run chronicles, if that is something you're genuinely interested in doing outside of mental exercise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T23:14:39-07:00","id":1063754,"title":"","content":"Dang, I would have liked to read the rest of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T04:37:31-07:00","id":1063808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063737#post1063737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you mind giving an example for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>There have been a few already, but to simply have someone kill a person who has means, and motive for doing it already with a modifying factor like drugs or alcohol. If you lay the groundwork properly then that's enough obscuring information that the players won't feel the need to investigate further. Though if they did they'd find that the alcohol was literally a bottle of spirits, the possession lasting just as long as the effects of the alcohol which has already left the killer's system by the time the Mages catch up with him. You're just looking to create a scenario that appears to confirm the player's bias either by layering information such that the answer seems obvious and no further investigation is required or by providing enough conflicting evidence that constructing a true account of what happened becomes difficult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">While real people in the real world can and do ignore the absolute truth in favor of their pre-conconceptions, a player that shoot themselves on the leg to that level is rare and not a measuring stick by any means.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>This is just too bizarre, you don't think players are real people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As for this thread original question, lower case mysteries arent a story you can really tell in mage unless either</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A) You go full plot convenience as </span></span></span><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2309\" data-vbnamecard=\"2309\">Ashenrogue</a><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> went and put high concept things like Irises.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">B) Nerf mages.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>This is a bogus claim. 1) Seen it done, 2) Done it myself, 3) Didn't need plot device or to nerf mages. What the heck do you think a mystery story is? Because as far as I know it's just a story with a question at the beginning, &quot;Whodunnit?&quot; and an answer at the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-17-2017, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T05:32:29-07:00","id":1063815,"title":"","content":"I see this like an episode of Columbo vs other crime shows, you get shown who the killer is at the start in Columbo then spend the rest of the show watching Columbo prove it.<br /> <br /> Same with Mages, Yes mages can piss all over your standard murder mystery but the story then becomes what do they do about it. You know the how, where and maybe even why, but what are you going to do about it? That'll be an intresting story right? Even if its as simple as &quot;I'll tell the Consilium and let them deal with it&quot; there will be ripples, you'll need to testify, perhaps the killer will come after you next? (you may or may not see it coming but then its again what do you do about it?)<br /> <br /> Also i see &quot;I look back in time and use mage sight on it&quot; a lot, how much information is mage sight really giving to help solve stuff? You see what happens via times postcog, you can then do what exactly? Ive only skimmed 2nd edtion mage sight as every time i try to read it i cant seem to think of real world examples of its use? Perhaps some examples would help?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T07:19:42-07:00","id":1063838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063750#post1063750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a Play By Post subforum in the Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play board where people run chronicles, if that is something you're genuinely interested in doing outside of mental exercise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure how I missed that being there. Anyways, not sure I'm ready to run a full blown online chronicle at the moment. It was fun enough as a spontaneous lets do this kinda thing but I'm not sure how dedicated I'd be passed that at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T09:16:42-07:00","id":1063894,"title":"","content":"Sorry, was called away by life events and then night happened. Guess we won't be continuing the AP :P<br /> Anyway. As someone who's been Storytelling Mage for a decade I find people's lack of imagination for obstacles annoying \u2013 a storyteller deciding that an Arcana is OP and then refusing any advice on how to handle it is, to put into terms that won't get me banned, frustrating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T09:28:10-07:00","id":1063901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063894#post1063894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a storyteller deciding that an Arcana is OP and then refusing any advice on how to handle it is, to put into terms that won't get me banned, frustrating.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a pretty good word choice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think what it comes down to is that ST-ing Mage is, in fact, <i>hard</i>, and does indeed require a lot of imagination. It requires a lot of imagination both on the part of the players and on the ST. Personally, I don't think Awakening is as hard on the players or the ST as Ascension is, but it's still pretty hard. I really think 2e has done a good job with making a bit more user friendly, but it's easily the least user friendly of the CofD. There's nothing <i>wrong </i>with that, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T09:42:17-07:00","id":1063908,"title":"","content":"OPP and WW games are pretty intricate, yeah. It's why I love them, even after years and years one still finds new combos and tricks and inspirations for homebrew.<br /> It's not the first time this happens either, every now and then people come by with similar threads about Fate, Mind, Forces and Space.<br /> It's like Overwatch players seeing their first Bastion on defense and concluding that the game must be broken because they can't find a way around it. All you can really say is... &quot;git gud&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 03-17-2017, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T01:40:30-07:00","id":1064218,"title":"","content":"I'm here with Dark Archon here. You cannot run more that scene or two of Time casting and not find all the Banishers or Scelesti done with victim. ( Unless antagonist not using Prime or Time - but how many Dark Mages can have those? All of them? ) I really would want example that mid Tier Banisher ( up to one Arcana on 4, but not Time or Prime higher than 3 ) to not be find in only few castings by 3-5 Paths cabal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T05:39:47-07:00","id":1064262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063647#post1063647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because mages play rocket tag. It really isn't that hard for one mage to kill another, and you had absolutely nothing up to stop soooo many forms of instagibbing you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't part of current thread, but I don't like this. It makes it virtually impossible to have chronicles or scenes about mages actually fighting each other, because it ends with TPK the exact moment enemy gets an upper hand in intelligence. How can I have a Banisher chronicle, if said Banishers just obliterate players with ease? How it can be interesting, if players obliterate Banishers with ease?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063647#post1063647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's pretty much no way to track them down for a single murder.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's just another limit of spectrum. According to you, uncovered mage crimes is downright impossible, which makes a whole parts of game redundant. How can Guardians of the Veil police mages, if they can't track the killers down? Why don't Seers destroy all mages, if they have upper hand in intelligence gathering, and killing other mage is trivial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 03-18-2017, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T05:55:39-07:00","id":1064266,"title":"","content":"Don't worry, your Acanthus will rewind the day in which your group got TPKed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T06:25:24-07:00","id":1064269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064266#post1064266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't worry, your Acanthus will rewind the day in which your group got TPKed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless enemy Acanthus stabilise the moment of death in time. Or Acanthus is the first target (which is logical).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T06:35:21-07:00","id":1064271,"title":"","content":"Have you thought about moving your Mage games away from mage on mage conflict, and refocusing it on Mage vs World? Honest question. It helped me a lot, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T06:48:39-07:00","id":1064274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064271#post1064271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you thought about moving your Mage games away from mage on mage conflict, and refocusing it on Mage vs World?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and personally I just don't see how World can threaten mages. Like, at all. The only really viable antagonists for Mages are other Mages, and that is inevitably lead to some type of magical combat.<br /> Besides, I love mage on mage conflict. There is a lot of great factions for that: Seers, Banishers, Scelesti, Liches\\Reapers - IMO the best parts of the setting. To ignore all that is to deny the setting the parts I love the most about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 03-18-2017, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T08:37:17-07:00","id":1064314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064218#post1064218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm here with Dark Archon here. You cannot run more that scene or two of Time casting and not find all the Banishers or Scelesti done with victim. ( Unless antagonist not using Prime or Time - but how many Dark Mages can have those? All of them? (</div> </div> </div> </div> And Death, don't forget Death's ability to destroy Sympathetic connections. Oh! And Mind's ability to cause the victim to go down a convoluted rabit hole that makes the investigation difficult, and also to veil observations by being with Mind. Double oh!! And also don't forget Spirit that can be used to get a disposable ephemeral hit man which is sent on two missions, kill the mage and then attack a bigger spirit which eats the assassin. ...<br /> <br /> Wait a minute! That covers all five Paths! Golly. And you next part of lumping Scelesti and Banasher together implies murder is the greatest threat of Scelesti, which it isn't. Moral/social/political/metaphysical corruption and increased abyssal intrussions are. Things much harder to track than mere murder. <br /> <br /> And as for Banashers who do murder mages, the book already states most die quickly, so it is safe to assume the survivors would be the ones with the above Toolbox, or tools I haven't thought of but serve the same purpose. Given just what is in this post covers the five paths and people can be more creative than you or I, it's very plausible some where there would be Banish\u00e8rs that have yet to find their match, in the same way in real life some serial killers have yet to be caught.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T08:39:32-07:00","id":1064315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064274#post1064274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and personally I just don't see how World can threaten mages. Like, at all. The only really viable antagonists for Mages are other Mages, and that is inevitably lead to some type of magical combat.<br /> Besides, I love mage on mage conflict. There is a lot of great factions for that: Seers, Banishers, Scelesti, Liches\\Reapers - IMO the best parts of the setting. To ignore all that is to deny the setting the parts I love the most about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking like human beings, I think that mages don't pay full attenttion to all the threats that can kill them. The further you adventure into Mysteries, you get more influence, status, enemies, etc.<br /> But let's get to the point on the mage vs mage where 1 mage is going missing or murdered.<br /> <br /> That alone is a lot of work to the play characters. Let's see my little list:<br /> <br /> A) They have to discover that the killer was a mage, wich can be a little difficult if the killer uses some spells to do it via proxy. Or to erase his presence. Remembering that the use of Rotes is extremely helpful to disguise Signature Nimbus.<br /> <br /> B) They discovered the enemy. Now what? Did the enemy discovered them as well? Did he had real motives to do what he did? If he is a mage, he problably has his magic defenses. Maybe he has a group of sorts as well, how powerfull is the enemy? And the mages will go blindly against the enemy? The local politics can help or hinder.<br /> <br /> There is a plot hook on Glimpses of the Unknown where the killer was a bunch of werewolfs that killed the mage cause they think that the mage has destroyed a Loci. And the plot is really great.<br /> Discovering who did it usually don't take that long, but what really consumes time is: &quot;What do?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T09:11:59-07:00","id":1064330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064314#post1064314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Death, don't forget Death's ability to destroy Sympathetic connections.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have missed one - can you point direct spell in corebook on this? It would kill both Temporal and Spacial Sympathy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064314#post1064314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! And Mind's ability to cause the victim to go down a convoluted rabit hole that makes the investigation difficult, and also to veil observations by being with Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not understand any of this - could you written this example in simpler English maybe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064314#post1064314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Double oh!! And also don't forget Spirit that can be used to get a disposable ephemeral hit man which is sent on two missions, kill the mage and then attack a bigger spirit which eats the assassin. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>So Spirits controlling Banisher sends <b>two</b> Shadow Realm spirits to kill target? I'm getting it right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064314#post1064314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Given just what is in this post covers the five paths and people can be more creative than you or I, it's very plausible some where there would be Banish\u00e8rs that have yet to find their match, in the same way in real life some serial killers have yet to be caught.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, problem is that I, as ST, need to know <b><i>what</i></b> Banisher do to the initial victim in the story plot. I just do not like to hand-wave it with 'Oh, your Arcana do not work in way to detect it' outside of official rules. It's dickish move of ST and proves the point on Time Arcanum going to solve any mystery plot in one or two scenes. Above three Arcana ideas examples sounds promising...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-18-2017, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T09:15:57-07:00","id":1064333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064315#post1064315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking like human beings, I think that mages don't pay full attenttion to all the threats that can kill them. The further you adventure into Mysteries, you get more influence, status, enemies, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I do think the more power they get, the more they afraid to lose it and die to some assassination attempt - like all dictators do. That's acting like human being IMO - you take measures to ensure your safety in response for danger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064315#post1064315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Discovering who did it usually don't take that long, but what really consumes time is: &quot;What do?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but discovery part isn't where, which was the complaint in the original post.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T10:26:15-07:00","id":1064362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064330#post1064330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must have missed one - can you point direct spell in corebook on this? It would kill both Temporal and Spacial Sympathy?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would require Space or Time at 1 to be able to perceive Sympathetic connections, but Death can erode nearly anything that can be perceived.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Do not understand any of this - could you written this example in simpler English maybe?</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Mind can mess with your thoughts or observations, applications for using it to throw off investigators should be obvious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So Spirits controlling Banisher sends </span></span></span><b>two</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Shadow Realm spirits to kill target? I'm getting it right?</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>No, they send one spirit to kill an enemy and then send the spirit they used as a hit man to a certain doom so that it can't be tracked back to the Mage who commanded it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, problem is that I, as ST, need to know </span></span></span><b><i>what</i></b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Banisher do to the initial victim in the story plot. I just do not like to hand-wave it with 'Oh, your Arcana do not work in way to detect it' outside of official rules. It's dickish move of ST and proves the point on Time Arcanum going to solve any mystery plot in one or two scenes. Above three Arcana ideas examples sounds promising...</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>That isn't what he was saying. Also the Time arcana can't solve any mystery plot in one or two scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T10:29:35-07:00","id":1064365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064333#post1064333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but discovery part isn't where, which was the complaint in the original post.</div> </div> </div> </div>A short period of time spent making a discovery doesn't invalidate the discovery part of game enjoyment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T11:17:19-07:00","id":1064390,"title":"","content":"Just popping in to say I *highly* approve of the method of helpibg the OP with his issue and appreciate being witness to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T11:21:08-07:00","id":1064391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064262#post1064262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't part of current thread, but I don't like this. It makes it virtually impossible to have chronicles or scenes about mages actually fighting each other, because it ends with TPK the exact moment enemy gets an upper hand in intelligence. How can I have a Banisher chronicle, if said Banishers just obliterate players with ease? How it can be interesting, if players obliterate Banishers with ease?<br /> <br /> <br /> But that's just another limit of spectrum. According to you, uncovered mage crimes is downright impossible, which makes a whole parts of game redundant. How can Guardians of the Veil police mages, if they can't track the killers down? Why don't Seers destroy all mages, if they have upper hand in intelligence gathering, and killing other mage is trivial?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's the lead up and mystery that's supposed to be interesting. Combat for mages, like in real life, is typically fast and brutal, with victory often going to the side that strikes first and with the greatest amount of force. The trick is to be the one to strike first, and with you running around turning yourself into a giant beeping kill me sign by spamming magic for all to see, you pretty much made it a certainty that that advantage wasn't going to you. You went in with not the slightest bit of reservation or stealth, knowing (or at least suspecting, since you never actually found out whether he was dead or not) there was a mage killer around. That's suicide.<br /> <br /> Uncovering well executed mage crimes is nigh impossible if you're only trying to rely on 1 or 2 arcana to do so. The reason that a lot of people get caught is that, like IRL, the crime wasn't quite as well executed as they thought and they made a mistake somewhere down the line, which most starting Banishers do which is why most die quickly. You were so obsessed with Time being invincible (even though it was Space that did at least half of the heavy lifting for you) you hardly tried any other options, and chased after every obvious clue without really taking the time to have your cabal mates really dig deeper with their stuff. And I knew you would so I coddled a bit and gave you clear links to something relevant rather than just saying lolnope you see nothing all the time. Let me just say that the lack of Spirit and lack of higher Prime would have really kicked you guys in the teeth had I done a &quot;simple&quot; murder mystery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064218#post1064218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm here with Dark Archon here. You cannot run more that scene or two of Time casting and not find all the Banishers or Scelesti done with victim. ( Unless antagonist not using Prime or Time - but how many Dark Mages can have those? All of them? ) I really would want example that mid Tier Banisher ( up to one Arcana on 4, but not Time or Prime higher than 3 ) to not be find in only few castings by 3-5 Paths cabal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Lol, when did I ever say the antagonists were limited to the same restrictions as the players? I just said they weren't Masters and didn't have Time. That's it. I also never specified how many enemies they were dealing with. That said, don't get yourself in a twist, there were only like 2 1/2 antagonists and none of them were much stronger than the player characters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-18-2017, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T11:43:57-07:00","id":1064401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064391#post1064391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's the lead up and mystery that's supposed to be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are interesting, but it's not the reason to make everything else not interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064391#post1064391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combat for mages, like in real life, is typically fast and brutal, with victory often going to the side that strikes first and with the greatest amount of force. The trick is to be the one to strike first</div> </div> </div> </div>You start to see the problem? This isn't interesting to play. At all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064391#post1064391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and with you running around turning yourself into a giant beeping kill me sign by spamming magic for all to see, you pretty much made it a certainty that that advantage wasn't going to you.<br /> ...You went in with not the slightest bit of reservation or stealth, knowing (or at least suspecting, since you never actually found out whether he was dead or not) there was a mage killer around. That's suicide.</div> </div> </div> </div>The alternative is to sit and do nothing. You can't find anything while not looking, and you certainly can't find anything by not gathering clues and making an investigation. What you are saying is: &quot;You can't investigate magic crime, because that make you the target&quot;. Okay, but then you can just kill the entire Consilium one by one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064391#post1064391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uncovering well executed mage crimes is nigh impossible if you're only trying to rely on 1 or 2 arcana to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said you need only the Time to uncover mysteries, only that with Time you always can find the place and see what happened and then analyze it with other Arcana. And you didn't disproved it, because your example directly depended on &quot;lol, Postcognition don't work&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064390#post1064390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just popping in to say I *highly* approve of the method of helpibg the OP with his issue and appreciate being witness to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This didn't help me, not a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T12:02:36-07:00","id":1064409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064401#post1064401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are interesting, but it's not the reason to make everything else not interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> You start to see the problem? This isn't interesting to play. At all.<br /> <br /> <br /> The alternative is to sit and do nothing. You can't find anything while not looking, and you certainly can't find anything by not gathering clues and making an investigation. What you are saying is: &quot;You can't investigate magic crime, because that make you the target&quot;. Okay, but then you can just kill the entire Consilium one by one.<br /> <br /> <br /> I never said you need only the Time to uncover mysteries, only that with Time you always can find the place and see what happened and then analyze it with other Arcana. And you didn't disproved it, because your example directly depended on &quot;lol, Postcognition don't work&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd disagree that everything else isn't interesting.<br /> <br /> Magic is crazy powerful. If you aren't either prepared for exactly what you're walking in to you are going to die really quickly. That's just the nature of it. It gets really interesting when both sides are good enough to do that and have to think of workarounds on the fly. Yes, if you try to play mage exactly like you would werewolf and just casually walk in activated all your stuff (this probably isn't a very accurate description of werewolf but that's the line of the main 3 I'm least familiar with so bear with me) you're going to have a bad time. That isn't the kinda story this particular setting and these particular mechanics are here to tell.<br /> <br /> Or, you could be subtle. You could try not to draw magical attention to yourselves, you could try to act like you were actually investigating a scene in which someone didn't want you finding them out. Instead you do the equivalent of walking around the neighborhood of a crime scene with a loud speaker and announcing how you're totally looking for the guy who did it and that yes, it's us over here with the loud speaker, we're the ones not just going about our day but actively trying to find you murder guy! You said it yourself, you were <i>constantly </i> checking to see if you'd be attacked and tracking your friends movements in the past.<br /> <br /> And your theory directly relied on 'lol, postcognition always works'. Which it doesn't. There are many ways to get around it. Prime, Mind, any arcana that lets you operate in a frequency of twilight you don't have access to. There is no Path that doesn't have an answer. I mean at this point you'd pretty much have to say Time can track anyone down <i>as long as you are also proficient at every other arcana</i>. Which is a bit silly because of course having access to everything makes things much more manageable, especially if you go under the assumption (which was wrong, at least in this case) that your opponents aren't as proficient as you are.<br /> <br /> Edit: Hmmm, I think I'm being a bit heavy on the snark, I'll try to tone it down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-18-2017, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T12:29:22-07:00","id":1064420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064409#post1064409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic is crazy powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is one-side crazy powerful. Namely, the offense is vastly more powerful than the defense. You may argue that this is how it should be. Maybe. But this isn't interesting, because it all boils down to &quot;who strikes first&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064409#post1064409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, you could be subtle. You could try not to draw magical attention to yourselves, you could try to act like you were actually investigating a scene in which someone didn't want you finding them out. Instead you do the equivalent of walking around the neighborhood of a crime scene with a loud speaker and announcing how you're totally looking for the guy who did it and that yes, it's us over here with the loud speaker, we're the ones not just going about our day but actively trying to find you murder guy! You said it yourself, you were <i>constantly </i> checking to see if you'd be attacked and tracking your friends movements in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see how this is &quot;walking around the neighborhood of a crime scene with a loud speaker&quot; unless you imply the killer was continuously scrying all the places where his target has been... or my character directly. The first thing is outside of capabilities of average mage. In second thing, it doesn't matter what I do - I am in the sights anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064409#post1064409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And your theory directly relied on 'lol, postcognition always works'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did find the place of incident, didn't I? So - it worked. That's exactly what I argued for, and it worked as it should. It would even show me the moment of death, and it would give me capability to scrutinize it with Mage Sight for clues.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T12:40:03-07:00","id":1064426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064420#post1064420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is one-side crazy powerful. Namely, the offense is vastly more powerful than the defense. You may argue that this is how it should be. Maybe. But this isn't interesting, because it all boils down to &quot;who strikes first&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't really see how this is &quot;walking around the neighborhood of a crime scene with a loud speaker&quot; unless you imply the killer was continuously scrying all the places where his target has been... or my character directly. The first thing is outside of capabilities of average mage. In second thing, it doesn't matter what I do - I am in the sights anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> I did find the place of incident, didn't I? So - it worked. That's exactly what I argued for, and it worked as it should. It would even show me the moment of death, and it would give me capability to scrutinize it with Mage Sight for clues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the defense is also pretty damn strong, you just have to have it prepared. So while it often times boils down to who strikes first in cases where you're unprepared, mages should rarely be unprepared.<br /> <br /> Peripheral Mage Sight. You were constantly pinging the magical senses of every mage in the area. With that constant casting there was no way you weren't up to something. Had it been a ping or two every now and then it'd be a bit different, but doing it constantly makes it seem like you're either looking for something or really fucking around with something in that area, and with you doing it while on the move really narrows it down to probably just looking for something. A killer would be less likely to act on someone he thinks is just passing through than on someone he thinks might be actively on his trail.<br /> <br /> You found something alright. But honestly, since you never went in you don't know what you found. And here you are still assuming there was a moment of death for you to see. I never once said there was, of implied that anyone died. You never saw a body, never saw an actual attack. You went in with a lot of assumption and absolutely none of them were proven right as far as you would/could know. I didn't specify a lot of things in that run because I was hoping you would pick up on my vagueness rather than stubbornly holding onto what you <i>thought</i> you knew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-18-2017, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T12:44:36-07:00","id":1064428,"title":"","content":"I think I've lost track, what is the actual problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T12:47:11-07:00","id":1064430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064428#post1064428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I've lost track, what is the actual problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, but I'm having fun arguing about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T12:49:13-07:00","id":1064431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064426#post1064426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the defense is also pretty damn strong, you just have to have it prepared. So while it often times boils down to who strikes first in cases where you're unprepared, mages should rarely be unprepared.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless we are talking about Prime magic - no, not really. Direct damage is always inferior to &quot;save-or-suck&quot; spells, and those are resisted by Withstand, which is penetrated easily by ES. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064426#post1064426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Peripheral Mage Sight. You were constantly pinging the magical senses of every mage in the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what is problem with that? Assuming that there aren't enough mages to have a high change to bumping into each other onto the street?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064426#post1064426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A killer would be less likely to act on someone he thinks is just passing through than on someone he thinks might be actively on his trail.</div> </div> </div> </div>A killer is very unlikely to hand around the place of killng, unless this is a trap, and from where we go to another problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064426#post1064426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You found something alright. But honestly, since you never went in you don't know what you found. And here you are still assuming there was a moment of death for you to see. I never once said there was, of implied that anyone died. You never saw a body, never saw an actual attack. You went in with a lot of assumption and absolutely none of them were proven right as far as you would/could know.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thread was about murders by Mage. I still talk about murders by mage. You tell me &quot;okay, but there is Mysteries which can't be solved by Postcognition!&quot;. Sure there are. But this wasn't what I was talking about in the beginning and now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T12:55:00-07:00","id":1064435,"title":"","content":"Postcognition is useful for solving some murder mysteries. That's the problem?<br /> <br /> How is that in any way a real problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:02:59-07:00","id":1064441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064435#post1064435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Postcognition is useful for solving some murder mysteries. That's the problem?<br /> <br /> How is that in any way a real problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;problem&quot; is the OP generalizing from that to say that it solves all mysteries forever. And I'm not exagerating:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver#post1063365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is <b>literally </b>no crime you can't solve with Time magic as if you were on spot of murder.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:13:59-07:00","id":1064449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064431#post1064431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless we are talking about Prime magic - no, not really. Direct damage is always inferior to &quot;save-or-suck&quot; spells, and those are resisted by Withstand, which is penetrated easily by ES.<br /> <br /> <br /> And what is problem with that? Assuming that there aren't enough mages to have a high change to bumping into each other onto the street?<br /> <br /> <br /> A killer is very unlikely to hand around the place of killng, unless this is a trap, and from where we go to another problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> The thread was about murders by Mage. I still talk about murders by mage. You tell me &quot;okay, but there is Mysteries which can't be solved by Postcognition!&quot;. Sure there are. But this wasn't what I was talking about in the beginning and now.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Clashes aren't Withstand, and ES don't bypass those.<br /> <br /> The problem is that you singled yourself out as a target rather than a bystander. Assuming the supposed murderer was there, which he very well could have been, he would have noticed you bringing attention to yourself. And that's a problem precisely because you're giving them the option of getting in the first strike.<br /> <br /> Not necessarily. Checking to see if anyone was nosing around the scene of the crime from a distance is a good way to see if anyone is actually on their trail. And you obviously were. And with veiling effects and all of the indirect methods of watching someone it wouldn't have been too hard to do so with relative safety.<br /> <br /> You were talking about tracking down a murderer with Time, which easily translates to tracking down someone you <i>believe</i> to be a murderer with Time. Just because you may or may not be wrong doesn't change that the accuracy of the demonstration. Whether Jim died or not from where you got too doesn't matter. If I said he died after going a ways into the Iris, your actions would have been the same as if I had decided to not have him dead after going through.<br /> <br /> I'm also never going to tell you if he was murdered or not. Not now anyways. Had we continued you would have known, but since we stopped it isn't really relevant anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064435#post1064435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Postcognition is useful for solving some murder mysteries. That's the problem?<br /> <br /> How is that in any way a real problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Fata-Ku pointed out he was claiming Time could solve all mysteries forever. Which isn't true. You'd need more than just Time to solve a lot of things. Hell, as I pointed out, he needed Space almost as much as he needed Time. That isn't Time solving any and all mysteries, that's various arcana solving any and all mysteries, which I would agree with. Having access to <i>all</i> the arcana makes solving things a lot more doable than just having 1 or 2. It's all about covering all the bases. If you can do that, you can accomplish most things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-18-2017, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:17:09-07:00","id":1064451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064435#post1064435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Postcognition is useful for solving some murder mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is useful for solving absolute most of murder crimes (except those where Time Magic won't work as intended), even ones solved with magic. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:22:39-07:00","id":1064457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064451#post1064451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is useful for solving absolute most of murder crimes (except those where Time Magic won't work as intended), even ones solved with magic.</div> </div> </div> </div> Time can <i>help</i> no doubt. <i>Any</i> arcana can help. But it can't do everything by itself, none of them can. Which is what you originally claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-18-2017, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:25:28-07:00","id":1064461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064451#post1064451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is useful for solving absolute most of murder crimes (except those where Time Magic won't work as intended), even ones solved with magic. </div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having trouble understanding what you're saying here, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:28:09-07:00","id":1064462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064449#post1064449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Clashes aren't Withstand, and ES don't bypass those.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is lot of spells which are Withstood, and if you don't conveniently have a Arcana Shield, there won't be a Clash of Wills to protect you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064449#post1064449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that you singled yourself out as a target rather than a bystander.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if this is a trap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064449#post1064449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily. Checking to see if anyone was nosing around the scene of the crime from a distance is a good way to see if anyone is actually on their trail.</div> </div> </div> </div>And checking if anyone is watching the scene of the crime from a distance is a good way to track down whoever is connected with crime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064449#post1064449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you obviously were. And with veiling effects and all of the indirect methods of watching someone it wouldn't have been too hard to do so with relative safety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not going to help at all if murderer will check with Active Mage Sight, which can penetrate the shields.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064449#post1064449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You were talking about tracking down a murderer with Time, which easily translates to tracking down someone you <i>believe</i> to be a murderer with Time. Just because you may or may not be wrong doesn't change that the accuracy of the demonstration.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does. It worked just as intented until the moment you said &quot;well, your Postcognition won't work, because Iris&quot;. This is roughly equivalent for &quot;well, your Postcognition won't work, because enemy Time magic&quot;. Certainly no difference for me here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064449#post1064449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also never going to tell you if he was murdered or not. Not now anyways. Had we continued you would have known, but since we stopped it isn't really relevant anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>And given I am talking specifically about murders here, it means there is nothing to talk about anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:30:50-07:00","id":1064463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064457#post1064457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time can <i>help</i> no doubt. <i>Any</i> arcana can help. But it can't do everything by itself, none of them can. Which is what you originally claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I specifically did not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver#post1063365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time magic solves every mystery (<b>not Mystery</b>) ever with one dot?</div> </div> </div> </div>So your example, which is Mystery by definition with Iris and Time magic stopping working, isn't example to situations I talked about in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:31:53-07:00","id":1064464,"title":"","content":"Can you even Shield from Arcana as a whole, instead from a certain thematically coherent range of phenomena falling under it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:34:02-07:00","id":1064465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064464#post1064464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you even Shield from Arcana as a whole, instead from a certain thematically coherent range of phenomena falling under it?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can't, then there is literally no defense to speak about. If you can only protect yourself from heart attacks out of all mage attack spells out there - you can't protect yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:43:43-07:00","id":1064472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064462#post1064462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is lot of spells which are Withstood, and if you don't conveniently have a Arcana Shield, there won't be a Clash of Wills to protect you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Only if this is a trap.<br /> <br /> <br /> And checking if anyone is watching the scene of the crime from a distance is a good way to track down whoever is connected with crime.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not going to help at all if murderer will check with Active Mage Sight, which can penetrate the shields.<br /> <br /> <br /> It does. It worked just as intented until the moment you said &quot;well, your Postcognition won't work, because Iris&quot;. This is roughly equivalent for &quot;well, your Postcognition won't work, because enemy Time magic&quot;. Certainly no difference for me here.<br /> <br /> <br /> And given I am talking specifically about murders here, it means there is nothing to talk about anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I said. If you were going into a situation you know that you might break out into life of death combat you should either be subtle, or load up on shielding effects to Clash against everything. That's how mage combat works. Either you be sneaky and get the first attack in yourself, or you go in prepared for anything and everything. <br /> <br /> Which it could have turned into by the very act of your constantly checking. Every time you check the future you potentially change it, and constantly checking it constantly gives the option of it changing. <br /> <br /> That's assuming you have any idea how they're doing it and are prepared for it, and can figure out how they're even doing it first. They could be watching from Twilight, watching from Twilight, Invisible to your mind, having spirits and or ghosts spy for them, have a normal person spy for them, whether mind controlled or not, or any other number of things. And as demonstrated by the example play, you checked for pretty much <i>none of those</i>. And no, just saying 'I'm constantly checking' doesn't count unless you specify what you're checking for and all you said was checking to see if you were going to be attacked.<br /> <br /> Only if it is relevant. And you have, what? Time and Space? Even if you did, half the methods of detecting someone aren't actively magical, there's nothing to see through.<br /> <br /> It worked until I decided to stop coddling. I let you get to play for awhile and enjoy the experience before throwing you a curve ball. I could have done it from the start in all manner of ways but I let you have your fun before turning up the difficulty the slightest bit.<br /> <br /> You were talking murder mysteries. And assuming you believe something is a murder mystery, and treat it like a murder mystery, the example holds up exactly like it was a murder mystery. So everything up to where you gave up was absolutely valid regardless of what actually happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:44:53-07:00","id":1064475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064451#post1064451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is useful for solving absolute most of murder crimes (except those where Time Magic won't work as intended), even ones solved with magic. </div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think you could clarify this please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:47:48-07:00","id":1064479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064463#post1064463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I specifically did not.<br /> <br /> <br /> So your example, which is Mystery by definition with Iris and Time magic stopping working, isn't example to situations I talked about in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063374#post1063374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if killer is another mage? How the hell they can kill each other then, if tracking the killer down is trivial? How do Banishers without Time Magic even exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>You decided to bring in mages and argue that angle, which automatically makes the mystery a Mystery. Had you completely left out other forms of magic and only based this off of mundane mysteries you might have had a point, but as soon as you introduced mages shit got real, and you never changed your statement. So yes you did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:50:30-07:00","id":1064481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064464#post1064464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you even Shield from Arcana as a whole, instead from a certain thematically coherent range of phenomena falling under it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda? Spells like Mental Shield protects against all effects that target the mind, but even in cases where you can't you can still shield yourself against the most commonly used effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T14:39:06-07:00","id":1064498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064479#post1064479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">which automatically makes the mystery a Mystery</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really from my point of view. And yes, I still think that Postcognition greatly helps to understand most of mage crimes, provided it works correctly; most of them would be solved just by using it and various Mage Sights for understanding exactly what happened at the time of murder. Your example didn't disproved that a bit; it only showed that there is some Mysteries (which may or may not be connected to murder) which isn't solved by Postcognition alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T14:43:20-07:00","id":1064501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064498#post1064498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really from my point of view. And yes, I still think that Postcognition greatly helps to understand most of mage crimes, provided it works correctly; most of them would be solved just by using it and various Mage Sights for understanding exactly what happened at the time of murder. Your example didn't disproved that a bit; it only showed that there is some Mysteries (which may or may not be connected to murder) which isn't solved by Postcognition alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fail to see the problem.<br /> <br /> I mean, when you play a game, do you play the regular mundane stuff that everyone goes through everyday? Or the exceptional circumstances that a main character experiences in the throes of a gripping story?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T14:52:15-07:00","id":1064505,"title":"","content":"Mages are the great investigators of the WoD any player with half a brain beams at the power of postcognition but to say it solves every crime is a bit much. <br /> It sounds like the ST isn't trying hard enough, Ashenrogue's example was great if that was played for real face to face it would have taken at least an hour provided minimal player detour, more like three hours at my table. <br /> <br /> If a player of yours is using time to great effect, making the game to easy for themselves and crushing the plot. as the ST don't pull punches. the answer doesn't need to be TKO. <br /> <br /> What the Postcog sees doesn't need to be the truth, doesn't need to be clear, doesn't need to be easy, doesn't need to be with out risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T15:08:25-07:00","id":1064511,"title":"","content":"I can't help but feel like the argument here boils down to &quot;Time can auto-solve any Investigation except the ones it can't.&quot; Like, if you write off any investigation where Postcognition alone won't get you the answer as &quot;a Mystery, not a mystery&quot;, then <i>of course</i> Postcognition will be able to give you the answer to any mystery. That's not an argument, it's just a tautology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T15:11:10-07:00","id":1064514,"title":"","content":"That and Postcog still needs to deal with mundane issues such as stealth and misdirection. Hell, even just fog. Being able to see the past doesn't guarantee noticing details or spotting the sniper who only needs sensory range to set someone on fire from the inside. The Time mage won't have access to every single Arcana, so it's up to the ST to find ways to misdirect the players.<br /> <br /> Sure, if all your player does is spend and hour scrutinizing every possible thing in the scene, they might get to the bottom of everything. But at that point, the killer kills again, flies to another country, frames the players as Scelesti or just plain gets backup.<br /> <br /> Again: &quot;I know who did it&quot; isn't the end of the story. You have to <b>prove it</b> and <b>catch the perp</b>.<br /> But I guess that doesn't matter in games where vigilante justice is the norm and the Concilii take your word for it when you say &quot;oh yeah, I killed him because he killed my friend&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 03-18-2017, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T15:43:55-07:00","id":1064535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064498#post1064498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really from my point of view. And yes, I still think that Postcognition greatly helps to understand most of mage crimes, provided it works correctly; most of them would be solved just by using it and various Mage Sights for understanding exactly what happened at the time of murder. Your example didn't disproved that a bit; it only showed that there is some Mysteries (which may or may not be connected to murder) which isn't solved by Postcognition alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I disagree with how you define Mystery. If a mage is involved, using magic to kill and/or obscure the nature of the murder, it's a Mystery. If a mage is involved and for some reason chooses not to use magic to help them get away with a crime, then you're not dealing with a mage, you're dealing with an idiot who was likely to die fairly quickly with or without your interference.<br /> <br /> Though regardless, even you if you want to consider such a crime a lower case m mystery I've already given you examples of how Time could easily be beaten, using the methods you tried to employ. Thus, I demonstrated how Time couldn't solve all mysteries forever, proving your entire argument that it can wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-18-2017, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T15:44:21-07:00","id":1064536,"title":"","content":"At low gnosis Mage is rocket tag. A cabal of Gnosis 3+ Mages with a decent spread of Arcana can be an extremely tough nut to crack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T16:11:14-07:00","id":1064544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064481#post1064481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda? Spells like Mental Shield protects against all effects that target the mind, but even in cases where you can't you can still shield yourself against the most commonly used effects.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then I guess a standard procedure for each Cabal should be casting group targeted [it's a Single Reach] &quot;Shield from Arcana&quot; Shielding Spells with massive Duration on the whole Cabal, making sure that they are constantly protected against enemy Magic. Add a maxed out Wards and Signs to that and maybe Suppress Aura. And a Mind Shield, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T16:13:59-07:00","id":1064546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064544#post1064544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Then I guess a standard procedure for each Cabal should be casting group targeted [it's a Single Reach] &quot;Shield from Arcana&quot; Shielding Spells with massive Duration on the whole Cabal, making sure that they are constantly protected against enemy Magic. Add a maxed out Wards and Signs to that and maybe Suppress Aura. And a Mind Shield, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. If you aren't trying to hide and are going somewhere you know will be dangerous you load up on defense first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T16:15:51-07:00","id":1064548,"title":"","content":"I mean keeping this up permanently. There are very few drawbacks to doing so, especially if you can Combine spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T16:29:15-07:00","id":1064552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064548#post1064548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean keeping this up permanently. There are very few drawbacks to doing so, especially if you can Combine spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>This biggest problems are going to be social at that point. You're going to make a lot of mages nervous if you try to walk around armed to the teeth glowing like the sun with all the spells you're loaded down with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T16:34:55-07:00","id":1064554,"title":"","content":"Why aren't they also loaded up like that anyway? Sounds like a basic function of having a Cabal, honestly. Kinda like Magical Second Amendment. <br /> Also, Suppress Aura specifically makes you not look like Christmas Tree, as it hides every single spell effect from detection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T16:38:16-07:00","id":1064555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064554#post1064554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why aren't they also loaded up like that anyway? Sounds like a basic function of having a Cabal, honestly. Kinda like Magical Second Amendment..</div> </div> </div> </div>The Consilium in Texas is way ahead of you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T16:42:36-07:00","id":1064558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064554#post1064554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why aren't they also loaded up like that anyway? Sounds like a basic function of having a Cabal, honestly. Kinda like Magical Second Amendment.<br /> Also, Suppress Aura specifically makes you not look like Christmas Tree, as it hides every single spell effect from detection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of courtesy. Even in an armed society you don't walk around with loaded assault rifles and shotguns all day. It has the bad habit of instantly upgrading the stakes when something inedvitably comes to hostilities. If everyone needs to worry about upping their defenses they're less likely to instantly resort to violence once things get heated out of caution. If everybody is already fully loaded, you aren't going to really get much more prepared for war than this so you might as well fight it out, which is something consilia and mage society at large is specifically tailored to dissuade.<br /> <br /> Essentially, if you had to be prepared at every second of every day to fight for your life (or at least you felt like you did), then loading up on spells would be a great idea. Mage society is specifically constructed so that you don't feel that way, and are willing to settle things in mage court as it were. Same for regular society really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-18-2017, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T18:19:05-07:00","id":1065531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1064554#post1064554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why aren't they also loaded up like that anyway? Sounds like a basic function of having a Cabal, honestly. Kinda like Magical Second Amendment. <br /> Also, Suppress Aura specifically makes you not look like Christmas Tree, as it hides every single spell effect from detection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent question! Hey given the Second Amendment why don't you wear a ballistic plate kevlar vest and carry an AR 15?<br /> <br /> The answers likely have mage analogies, like it's locally restricted via law (local lex magica rulings), would make you a social pariah for several reasons:<br /> Shows you expect violence against your own person (that's pretty suspicious, what type of person expects to be attacked? Take moment to look around real life begore you answer)<br /> Show you are mentally prepared and capable of brutal violence if need be.<br /> Show you have no faith in the system of laws to protect you.<br /> Shows you have no faith in the authority figures set to defend you.<br /> It's horribly anti-social. <br /> <br /> The assumed status quo is that violence is a bad nieghorhood, bad city, or a third world problem for mundane western society at least, and just because you know the world is a Lie doesn't make you any less a product of your culture, even if you're a subculture counter movement. (Glances at all the Adamantine Arrow Sovereign Individual Militia gun nuts camped out in Montana) <br /> <br /> Also if you have a mage investigation team backed by the rest of the Colesium are after you as a killer the main way they don't catch you is if they give up trying to find the origin point of the Rosenberg murder plot, because its just too convoluted or they capture a pawn instead of you, satisfied justice was done.<br /> (Note said main way, not only way)<br /> <br /> Also Spirit or Mind or Death + Familiar &gt; Time because of the Omen, Pathfinder, and Seek Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-20-2017, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T23:14:40-07:00","id":1065602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063378#post1063378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit 2:<br /> &quot;You rewind and rewind. You see a man walking backwards, seeming uninteresting until you see him stare off in a direction and mutter something. You stop at the beginning of his sentence \u2013 maybe it's important \u2013 and come around, circling him in paused-time to size him up. He looks pale, angular. His eyes command a powerful presence. There's something in them. Not literally, of course, but there's something... deep. You stare and let go of your hold on time. The scene progresses. He whispers: &quot;Grab your friend and slit his throat&quot;.<br /> <br /> The order resonates in your skull.<br /> Roll Resolve + Composure.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is quite hilarious to me.<br /> <br /> I can see a vamp in the past moment looking away from his friends to a spot on the wall. Uttering the command and asking himself why did I just command the wall? With out context in the past it's nonsense, but vindicated when you pull the time spring back. It's either mythical guidance, amazing lucky guess work, and or raw experience. reminds of Malks so rarely done right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":11731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","user":"MercSet","date":".  spelling 03-21-2017, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T23:43:29-07:00","id":1065607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065602#post1065602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is quite hilarious to me.<br /> <br /> I can see a vamp in the past moment looking away from his friends to a spot on the wall. Uttering the command and asking himself why did I just command the wall? With out context in the past it's nonsense, but vindicated when you pull the time spring back. It's either mythical guidance, amazing lucky guess work, and or raw experience. reminds of Malks so rarely done right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember doing something similar to my players. They were spying via postcognition on a vampire riding the same train. The difference was that the vampire only said 'I see you' but they freaked out so hard. It was fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T00:19:01-07:00","id":1065610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065607#post1065607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember doing something similar to my players. They were spying via postcognition on a vampire riding the same train. The difference was that the vampire only said 'I see you' but they freaked out so hard. It was fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice I love little moments like these. They show a lot of buy in from the players to be in and play out the story. Definitely keeps them on edge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T01:36:16-07:00","id":1065633,"title":"","content":"Uses postcognition to observe the murder<br /> <br /> Oh god, it was Jeff the Wizard who did it! Book 'im Danno!<br /> <br /> But actually it was Gina the Witch, using magic to look like Jeff. Of course since postcognition solves all murder mysteries instantly, you'd have thought that this would be revealed, but it isn't.<br /> <br /> Turns out only an immensely stupid Mage commits murder and even lets you have the opportunity to cast postcognition at the crime scene, never mind does it obviously while there. They hide the body under layers of Fate and Space, or transform it to nothingness with Matter, incinerate it utterly with Forces, or leave it in the depths of the Shadow with Spirit, so nobody can even use powerful spells like postcognition, and if they did, you misdirected them with other magics!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T05:08:10-07:00","id":1065685,"title":"","content":"Eh, I wouldn't compare having a Mental Shield [or any other Shield] on you to being armed with heavy weaponry. You can't grab your Shielding spells and start shooting people with them. Shielding Spells don't increase your ability to threat people [you, as a Mage, are always loaded weapon platform]. I would rather compare it to having your iphone set to secure internet and wifi settings [so a random person wont just check it out], using a secure browser, not logging into your bank account on public computers and locking your car when you go to grab a burger. Or locking your house when you go to sleep or for a walk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T05:23:18-07:00","id":1065693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065685#post1065685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would rather compare it to having your iphone set to secure internet and wifi settings [so a random person wont just check it out], using a secure browser, not logging into your bank account on public computers and locking your car when you go to grab a burger. Or locking your house when you go to sleep or for a walk.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's much more obvious than a private device in your pocket which (mostly) only you get to look at. More like wearing a bullet-proof vest at school, at a wal-mart, etc. while <i>also</i> being a walking weapons platform.<br /> Doesn't inspire confidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T05:31:57-07:00","id":1065696,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar43_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"43\" data-vbnamecard=\"43\">Fata-Ku</a> <br /> <br /> I can see different cities see each spell usage differently. A city with an active city wide mind mystery would see a mental shield as prudent while life or forces shield is somewhat rude. and Infact I can see a city with a vampire population having death and mind shields as important as having an umbrella in England or Seattle","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T06:03:07-07:00","id":1065704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1063387#post1063387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have Time magic to track down the killed one. You just look at him in the past up to the moment when he died, and then you witness his death.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has all the limitations of a normal, real-time witnessing the murder, on top of a few new challenges.<br /> <br /> So. Can you conceive of a way to kill someone without a nearby mage noticing you did it? Then temporally that is still valid.<br /> <br /> Yes, mages are <b>hax</b> when it comes to unveiling mysteries (it's no accident they solve Mysteries instead of mysteries in their usual challenges). But you are overestimating that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T06:21:10-07:00","id":1065712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065696#post1065696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <br /> <br /> I can see different cities see each spell usage differently. A city with an active city wide mind mystery would see a mental shield as prudent while life or forces shield is somewhat rude. and Infact I can see a city with a vampire population having death and mind shields as important as having an umbrella in England or Seattle</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean sure, but I'd imagine that's more the exception than the rule, the kind of thing that would be brought up at Concilium because Sentinels need to all be on the same page about it, in the &quot;innocent people don't run&quot; (read: &quot;death-veil themselves&quot;) sense.<br /> <br /> Though honestly I'd totally be the kind of person to constantly walk around with Incognito Presence because i just want people to leave me alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T06:51:12-07:00","id":1065722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065685#post1065685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I wouldn't compare having a Mental Shield [or any other Shield] on you to being armed with heavy weaponry. You can't grab your Shielding spells and start shooting people with them. Shielding Spells don't increase your ability to threat people [you, as a Mage, are always loaded weapon platform]. I would rather compare it to having your iphone set to secure internet and wifi settings [so a random person wont just check it out], using a secure browser, not logging into your bank account on public computers and locking your car when you go to grab a burger. Or locking your house when you go to sleep or for a walk.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, peripheral mage sight, which is going to be their first impression of you, isn't going to differentiate between a bunch of shielding spells and a bunch of hung killing the shit out of you spells. All they see if a mage, decked out in a ton of active magical effects walking around pinging the shit out of their magical senses. And while they might be able to identify some as shielding spells (by having the arcana of said spell) they aren't going to be able to identify all of them (at least individually at a moments notice). <br /> <br /> It's comparable to walking around wearing a bomb suit or military grade combat armor. It is generally assumed that if you are wearing that kinda thing then you plan on, or see that it is likely that you are going to need/use it, and that makes people nervous. What kind of nut goes to grocery store to buy milk wearing 6 different layers of class 4 armor? The kind you probably don't want to associate with or want in your neighborhood around your kids.<br /> <br /> And again, this is the type of thing that leads to escalation of violence and is frowned upon by society. Sure, a Mental Shield here, or a Mage Armor there would be relatively acceptable, but anything more than that makes it seem like you're actively looking for trouble. It's like wearing riot gear in real life. You might not really be able to hurt people with the gear itself, but it allows you to strike at others with little fear of any sort of defensive retaliation because they can't effectively do much to get through your armor, which leads to an escalation as they then begin preparing increased offenses just in case you do try something just to get through your defenses. Simply put, it leads to a bit of an arms race that mage society is trying its damnedest to prevent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T06:56:32-07:00","id":1065727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065722#post1065722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it allows you to strike at others with little fear of any sort of defensive retaliation because they can't effectively do much to get through your armor</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't even remotely the case with Mage Armor.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T07:03:04-07:00","id":1065732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065727#post1065727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't even remotely the case with Mage Armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence why he's talking about defensive spells and not Mage armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T07:25:40-07:00","id":1065748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065732#post1065732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hence why he's talking about defensive spells and not Mage armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't the case with defensive spells either. You can burn through Clash of Wills with attack spell. It depends on luck, but this is most certainly not &quot;<i>allows you to strike at others with little fear of any sort of defensive retaliation&quot;.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T07:30:42-07:00","id":1065751,"title":"","content":"Somebody walking around with Wards and Signs (prime 2) at potency 7* (not that hard to achieve for an adept or a master, just +2 or 3 potency) is walking around with a sign that says &quot;I remove 7 Potency from anyone casting on me&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which is basically walking around in riot gear.<br /> <br /> * I use 7 as a slightly-extreme example, because traits don't generally go that high, but just having it on is suspicious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 03-21-2017, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T07:38:15-07:00","id":1065756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065751#post1065751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somebody walking around with Wards and Signs (prime 2) at potency 7 (not that hard to achieve for an adept or a master, just +2 or 3 potency) is walking around with a sign that says &quot;I remove 7 Potency from anyone casting on me&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which is basically walking around in riot gear.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, +3 Potency is -6 to dicepool. Not that hard, but isn't trivial either. Second, that's pretty specific situation - it requires an Adept of Prime and specific prime spell. Third, you are still vulnerable to indirect spells, so your riot gear still won't help against air around you suddenly becoming an fire, gravity smashing you into the ceiling and so on. So you are still fully open to defensive retaliation, but defending side should be a little more creative with their power. And, incidentally, most Mages are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T07:42:27-07:00","id":1065758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065756#post1065756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, +3 Potency is -6 to dicepool. Not that hard, but isn't trivial either. Second, that's pretty specific situation - it requires an Adept of Prime and specific prime spell. Third, you are still vulnerable to indirect spells, so your riot gear still won't help against air around you suddenly becoming an fire, gravity smashing you into the ceiling and so on. So you are still fully open to defensive retaliation, but defending side should be a little more creative with their power. And, incidentally, most Mages are.</div> </div> </div> </div>So? The point is that defensive spells cause people to be weary of you, not whether they can be bypassed or not.<br /> <br /> The simple fact of erecting a shield that contests people's casting implies that you're expecting people to cast on you. Whether or not it's because you're going to be attacking them is left as an open question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T07:47:17-07:00","id":1065761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065758#post1065758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is that defensive spells cause people to be weary of you, not whether they can be bypassed or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really think that depends on Storyteller and Consilium in question. Personally, I think that mages have enough antagonists and dangers after them so most of them keep some Shielding spells literally always. It is a wise precaution in the world where you can't really be safe, ever. And if everybody wears the armor, then it is a custom and people don't mind it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T08:24:41-07:00","id":1065779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065748#post1065748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't the case with defensive spells either. You can burn through Clash of Wills with attack spell. It depends on luck, but this is most certainly not &amp;quot;<i>allows you to strike at others with little fear of any sort of defensive retaliation&amp;quot;.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly would allow you to strike at an opponent with less fear of retaliation though. That's the point of defensive magic after all. The point is too fine to really matter though, the perceived rudeness or threat of wearing defensive spells on your person is going to come down to custom and interpersonal politics as you pointed out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T08:32:31-07:00","id":1065788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065722#post1065722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of nut goes to grocery store to buy milk wearing 6 different layers of class 4 armor?</div> </div> </div> </div>The kind of nut who joined a cult of people fighting agaisnt the servants of the concept of tyranny and the concept themselves in a sort of cold war in which their magic system is such a rocket tag? That kind of nut.<br /> <br /> Even then, we dont usually wear ballistic armor in dangerous neighborhoods because its both expensive and cumbersome but magic is neither. If you live in part of town in which people get shoot regularly and armor was no more cheap or cumbersome than a tshirt then why wouldnt you wear it?<br /> <br /> Kinda the same thing with shadowrun, in which one has to assume 90% of the people wear armored clothing because is incredible cheap and barely any more heavy that the non-ballistic version of the clothes in question.<br /> <br /> I get what you saying but the game is kinda iffy about what is and what isnt normal social behavior among mages. Some fluff paint them in a constant state of paranoia in which the seers/banishers/scelesti are gonna control your love ones, steal your soul, rewrite your personal time line/fate/adn or all of them if you mess up. Other dont, i particularly remember a fluff piece that showed how stressful was to have perma magic shield 24/7 but neither then nor now is there any mechanic to back that up.<br /> <br /> I can perfectly see mages light up as Christmas trees to mage sight by shieldings alone. Not to mention any other kind of functional spell they would need for &quot;every day&quot; stuff like a life effect to cure some sickness or something else not related to combat/defending.<br /> <br /> In your example of normal people not wearing ballistic armor in every day life is a false comparison, the better example would be &quot;Would someone wear antirocket armor (assuming it existed) in a society in which instead of gun we got rocket launchers, everyone is equipped with one and we got a millenial old cold war going on in which the enemy could be around us?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 03-21-2017, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T09:04:18-07:00","id":1065813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065788#post1065788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The kind of nut who joined a cult of people fighting agaisnt the servants of the concept of tyranny and the concept themselves in a sort of cold war in which their magic system is such a rocket tag? That kind of nut.</div> </div> </div> </div>If only there were some obvious mitigating factor at play, like obvious magic being harder to control in front of the vast majority of humanity, casting being substantially easier to succeed at when accompanied by obvious props and activities, and maintaining a mortal identity separate from your magical one making it harder to track you down in the former based on similarity to the latter. Then there might be a reason for characters to go out in public under the assumption that they wouldn't have to worry about incoming spells any more than an average bystander has to worry about bullets \u2014 some sort of handy excuse for newer mages to keep active in mortal society and for old mages to be reclusive and inclined to take apprentices and send them out on errands.<br /> <br /> Would that this were the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T10:41:41-07:00","id":1065846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065813#post1065813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If only there were some obvious mitigating factor at play, like obvious magic being harder to control in front of the vast majority of humanity, casting being substantially easier to succeed at when accompanied by obvious props and activities, and maintaining a mortal identity separate from your magical one making it harder to track you down in the former based on similarity to the latter. Then there might be a reason for characters to go out in public under the assumption that they wouldn't have to worry about incoming spells any more than an average bystander has to worry about bullets \u2014 some sort of handy excuse for newer mages to keep active in mortal society and for old mages to be reclusive and inclined to take apprentices and send them out on errands.<br /> <br /> Would that this were the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>If only that mechanic wasnt toothless and casting from your sactum and sniping wasnt stupidly easy. Would that this were the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T10:46:41-07:00","id":1065849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065813#post1065813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If only there were some obvious mitigating factor at play, like obvious magic being harder to control in front of the vast majority of humanity</div> </div> </div> </div>Legacies with their Attainments. Also, non-obvious magic can still be very, very deadly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065813#post1065813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">casting being substantially easier to succeed at when accompanied by obvious props and activities</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of them are perfectly transportable. Incidentally, they also give the biggest amount of bonuses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T11:02:16-07:00","id":1065852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065849#post1065849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legacies with their Attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;It doesn't work if you have someone who has bent their magical identity toward the express purpose of ruining you&quot; is not so much a counterargument as an admission of defeat \u2014 the vast majority of mages one is likely to encounter are not going to be magical assassins with a grudge against you in particular, and the vast majority of mages is what this chunk of the discussion is supposedly about, not mages who are the subject of a personal vendetta.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, non-obvious magic can still be very, very deadly. </div> </div> </div>And the same mechanical channel that makes your Persona tools more effective also makes it harder to affect you and find you when you're not in a position to use them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of them are perfectly transportable. Incidentally, they also give the biggest amount of bonuses. </div> </div> </div>The three biggest bonuses come from extradimensional reagents you had to put notable effort into acquiring, being part of a group of mages who are all as invested in their defined magical personas as it's possible to be, and being highly trained in the right Skill for a given individual spell. That these are mobile does not make them indistinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T11:02:29-07:00","id":1065853,"title":"","content":"Having specifically played a Mage detective who made copious use of Postcognition, its honestly a lot less useful than it seems if the mystery afoot is any more complex than a simple game of Clue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T11:18:12-07:00","id":1065863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065685#post1065685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I wouldn't compare having a Mental Shield [or any other Shield] on you to being armed with heavy weaponry. You can't grab your Shielding spells and start shooting people with them. Shielding Spells don't increase your ability to threat people [you, as a Mage, are always loaded weapon platform]. I would rather compare it to having your iphone set to secure internet and wifi settings [so a random person wont just check it out], using a secure browser, not logging into your bank account on public computers and locking your car when you go to grab a burger. Or locking your house when you go to sleep or for a walk.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065531#post1065531\">So just the Ballistic Plate Kevlar Vest and no rifle then?</a><br /> of course that is referring to protection against physical assault, which you're correct isn't the same as protection against invasions of privacy.<br /> <br /> I am in agreement with the Mental Shield, because a mind is a terrible thing to be hacked. But there is a reasonable line in what investigation counter measures are acceptable in real life, and I'd expect a similar line in the fictional world<br /> <br /> I'd say using TOR would be a be an internet equivalent to the anonymity offered by magic. You could wear a mask to protect you from being filmed by the hundreds of cameras that take <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=how+many+times+a+day+am+i+photographed&amp;ie=utf-8&amp;oe=utf-8\" target=\"_blank\">your picture every day for walking down the street. </a>Or having a wallet that <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=wallet+that+prevents+magnetic+chip+readers&amp;ie=utf-8&amp;oe=utf-8\" target=\"_blank\">prevents magnetic chip readers</a>. Or wearing latex gloves everywhere so people can't get your finger prints.Or removing your license plate so traffic cameras can't track you.<br /> <br /> That type of behavior is still outside of social norm, for similar reasons as my previous linked post...<br /> <br /> It has been said magic amplifies mundane things, and that's true for investigation and I would say also true for investigation counter measures. The second one carrying stigma's for valid reasons.<br /> <br /> Question what would you think about someone who does all those mundane measures &quot;to defend themselves&quot;? What would a common person think?<br /> <br /> Where is the line between reasonable privacy and paranoia in the real world? How would that translate to amplified abilities on both side of investigation and investigation counter measures?<br /> I think this is all very interesting, from a sociological point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-21-2017, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:00:58-07:00","id":1065878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065852#post1065852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It doesn't work if you have someone who has bent their magical identity toward the express purpose of ruining you&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of Legacy do have at least one Attainment which can be used offensively, and all of them can be with some preparation for conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065852#post1065852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the vast majority of mages one is likely to encounter are not going to be magical assassins with a grudge against you in particular</div> </div> </div> </div>The vast majority of mages one is likely to encounter are not going to try and murder your in the open. Those who will try, though, will have a plan for not getting hit with Paradox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065852#post1065852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The three biggest bonuses come from extradimensional reagents you had to put notable effort into acquiring, being part of a group of mages who are all as invested in their defined magical personas as it's possible to be, and being highly trained in the right Skill for a given individual spell. That these are mobile does not make them indistinct.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they do make casting substantially easier to succeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:02:28-07:00","id":1065879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065863#post1065863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is the line between reasonable privacy and paranoia in the real world? </div> </div> </div> </div>It hardly matters. Mages have <i>reasons </i>to be paranoid - they have most of the facts, and those facts are <i>terrifying</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:14:14-07:00","id":1065884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065878#post1065878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of Legacy do have at least one Attainment which can be used offensively, and all of them can be with some preparation for conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>And those Legacies are not generic phenomena and their Attainments do not have the scalable advantages of spellcraft.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The vast majority of mages one is likely to encounter are not going to try and murder your in the open. Those who will try, though, will have a plan for not getting hit with Paradox. </div> </div> </div>The context in which one has given another mage reason to want to murder them, in the open or otherwise, is not one that lends a character to treat loading up on defensive spells as a casual activity, particularly when mage society regularly breaks itself into alliances that render the political fallout of a cabalmate's sudden disappearance more troublesome than most mages are prepared to deal with without substantial preparation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But they do make casting substantially easier to succeed. </div> </div> </div>Which is not under contention. Dressing or acting in the sort of unusual manner generally necessitated by magical Instruments provides tells that point to the character that uses them, particularly with things as individualized as a persona or as formalized as a mudra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:33:55-07:00","id":1065891,"title":"","content":"<br /> Originally posted by <b>Pale_Crusader</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065863#post1065863\">View Post</a><br /> Where is the line between reasonable privacy and paranoia in the real world?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065879#post1065879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It hardly matters. Mages have <i>reasons </i>to be paranoid - they have most of the facts, and those facts are <i>terrifying</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are <i><u>reasons</u> </i>to be paranoid in real life, that's why some people are. Real life is terrifying if you allow yourself to fully fathom the certain facts and probabilities that could snuff you out like a candle in a hurricane. Paranoid people are still stigmatized because they don't filter that out and let those thoughts affect their actions.<br /> <br /> Paranoia isn't safe, for those around the paranoid person and for the paranoid person, as counter intuitive as that seems. It can easily make you a danger to yourself and others.<br /> <br /> If the implication is that humans knowing danger exist compels them to take &quot;reasonable&quot; counter measures, please explain people not wearing seat belts, posting their personal information for public display online (facebook), txting while driving, and not for preparing natural disasters when they live in a place known for natural disasters?<br /> <br /> Mages surely wouldn't be immune to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akrasia\" target=\"_blank\">Akrasia</a> and <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_swan_theory\" target=\"_blank\">Black </a><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_swan_theory\" target=\"_blank\">Swan Theory </a>which are driving factors in complacent social norms assuming safety.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065884#post1065884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The context in which one has given another mage reason to want to murder them, in the open or otherwise, is not one that lends a character to treat loading up on defensive spells as a casual activity, particularly when mage society regularly breaks itself into alliances that render the political fallout of a cabalmate's sudden disappearance more troublesome than most mages are prepared to deal with without substantial preparation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well put. +1 Internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-21-2017, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:57:04-07:00","id":1065902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065879#post1065879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It hardly matters. Mages have <i>reasons </i>to be paranoid - they have most of the facts, and those facts are <i>terrifying</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Pale_Crusader pointed out, <i>everyone</i> has reasons to be paranoid. Even in real life. Let me ask you, do you personally prepare extensively for every potential danger that might come your way at all times? If the answer is no, why not? You have reasons to do so. How many people do you know who do? If the answer isn't everyone or even most, why not? They too have reason to be paranoid. Every reason or excuse you can possibly think of as to why people don't act in such a manner probably also applies to mages to some degree or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T13:15:00-07:00","id":1065907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065891#post1065891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real life is terrifying if you allow yourself to fully fathom the certain facts and probabilities that could snuff you out like a candle in a hurricane.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is probability. For people living in lawful and calm community probability to get violently killed is low, which is why they don't think about it and get by just fine. For people living in bad place with crime probability to get violently killed is higher, which is why they take precautions - move out of this place, or don't walk around late and have some way to defend themselves.<br /> We are talking about World of Darkness, where every place is bad place. And mages can't even take refuge in ignoring things. They know things are bad, and they know exactly how bad those things are. The probability of careless mage to live long is the same as probability of surviving battlefield by walking around naked and not take cover. Which isn't very low.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065891#post1065891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the implication is that humans knowing danger exist compels them to take &quot;reasonable&quot; counter measures, please explain people not wearing seat belts, posting their personal information for public display online (facebook), txting while driving, and not for preparing natural disasters when they live in a place known for natural disasters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't such people seen as careless and stupid? I certainly do see every person who do the things above as stupid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065902#post1065902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me ask you, do you personally prepare extensively for every potential danger that might come your way at all times?</div> </div> </div> </div>After probability of such event becomes too high in my opinion? Yes, I do. And all people I know do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T13:32:07-07:00","id":1065914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065907#post1065907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is probability. For people living in lawful and calm community probability to get violently killed is low, which is why they don't think about it and get by just fine. For people living in bad place with crime probability to get violently killed is higher, which is why they take precautions - move out of this place, or don't walk around late and have some way to defend themselves.<br /> We are talking about World of Darkness, where every place is bad place. And mages can't even take refuge in ignoring things. They know things are bad, and they know exactly how bad those things are. The probability of careless mage to live long is the same as probability of surviving battlefield by walking around naked and not take cover. Which isn't very low.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aren't such people seen as careless and stupid? I certainly do see every person who do the things above as stupid.<br /> <br /> <br /> After probability of such event becomes too high in my opinion? Yes, I do. And all people I know do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probability of being randomly killed isn't really that much higher for a mage, so by that logic they should generally be as heavily geared/cautious as the average Sleeper in their region. It isn't until mages start digging into things that are usually knowingly dangerous that problems arise, and in that situation it makes sense to prepare, because the probability <i>is</i> high.<br /> <br /> But doing so constantly, even when going about their normal lives, because mages <i>do</i> have normal lives, is probably going to be seen as abnormal. There's <i>very rarely</i> going to be someone who is in danger <i>all the time</i> and it's honestly better to avoid those people as a general rule of thumb. So when going about business as usual, doing normal research, taking a stroll around town, going on a date, going out to eat, etc., being geared up as if you were about to go to war is still a pretty big social stigma. It's weird, uncommon for most, and again, makes people nervous, because if you're <i>that</i> prepared for trouble, who knows what sort of trouble you have following you.<br /> <br /> You've got to remember that mages, while they get into some weird shit sometimes, are for the most part normal humans. Anyone can Awaken, they comes in all stripes. A younger sibling, a mother of 4, a janitor, an blue collar office worker. These people aren't all trained adventurers, badass commandos, or what have you. These are normal people with magic. Obsessive normal people with magic, but still just people. It's actually one of the reasons Seer recruitment is so easy. They're just regular people, so offering all the things that a regular person could ever want just to join their side is something that really works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-21-2017, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T13:41:18-07:00","id":1065918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065914#post1065914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probability of being randomly killed isn't really that much higher for a mage</div> </div> </div> </div>Average sleeper isn't hunted by Seers, Banishers, Tremere, other Reapers, Scelesti, hunters and everyone else at once.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065914#post1065914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's <i>very rarely</i> going to be someone who is in danger <i>all the time</i></div> </div> </div> </div><i>All </i>mages in danger <i>all </i>the time. That goes with being a mage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T13:42:24-07:00","id":1065920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065907#post1065907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are talking about World of Darkness, where every place is bad place. </div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, you are talking about Chronicles of Darkness, where every place is a mysterious place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T13:45:50-07:00","id":1065921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065920#post1065920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, you are talking about Chronicles of Darkness, where every place is a mysterious place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and some the times those Mysteries are active hostile. Other times, they are passively hostile, or just dangerous.<br /> But the point isn't about the mysteries, it's about reality which is ruled by god-tyrants who actively doing their best to make humanity as miserable as possible. But somehow it is still safe in the streets and people aren't afraid to go in the night without a weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 03-21-2017, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T13:52:17-07:00","id":1065927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065921#post1065921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, and some the times those Mysteries are active hostile. Other times, they are passively hostile, or just dangerous.<br /> But the point isn't about the mysteries, it's about reality which is ruled by god-tyrants who actively doing their best to make humanity as miserable as possible. But somehow it is still safe in the streets and people aren't afraid to go in the night without a weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And some times the mysteries are just mysterious, not dangerous at all. Or are even positive.<br /> <br /> And some of the Exarchs also want people to be happy, not just miserable. As long as they are controlled and know it (depends on the Exarch).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T13:55:28-07:00","id":1065928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065918#post1065918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Average sleeper isn't hunted by Seers, Banishers, Tremere, other Reapers, Scelesti, hunters and everyone else at once.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>All </i>mages in danger <i>all </i>the time. That goes with being a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Average Awakened aren't actively hunted by Seers, Banishers, Tremere, other Reapers, Scelesti, hunters and everyone else at once either. I think you're mistaking the oddly active lives of PCs as being exactly the same as everyone else in the world. Most people, mages included, <i>aren't</i> constantly in danger (at least no more so than most people are anyways). Not to say that they're <i>never</i> in danger, but the probability is generally low enough that, like people in real life, they don't need to be constantly on guard and geared out the teeth.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind how few mages there actually are in the setting. You're more likely to run into a Sleeper serial killer or the like than you are a Banisher, Scelesti or whatever assuming you aren't knowingly putting yourself out there for them to really notice. And how extensively do you or anyone else you know of prepare for encountering those? Sure, you might take basic precautions, which most mages do (hence one or two defensive measures not being that unexpected), but most people aren't going to go full on doomsday prepper, and the people who do are looked at funny and face social stigma.<br /> <br /> Edit: Now do take into consideration that I'm not necessarily arguing that they would be completely <i>wrong</i> in doing so and loading up on defenses. I'm just pointing out that they almost certainly will be looked at funny and face said social stigma in any community not currently/recently under siege by some sort of enemy/menace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-21-2017, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T14:04:26-07:00","id":1065934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065918#post1065918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Average sleeper isn't hunted by Seers, Banishers, Tremere, other Reapers, Scelesti, hunters and everyone else at once.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Holy shit!</i> What the fuck did you do to get all of them after you at the same time!?<br /> <br /> I do believe that mages are in a lot more danger than the average Sleeper but you're approaching the other extreme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T14:10:51-07:00","id":1065935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065928#post1065928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Average Awakened aren't actively hunted by Seers, Banishers, Tremere, other Reapers, Scelesti, hunters and everyone else at once either. I think you're mistaking the oddly active lives of PCs as being exactly the same as everyone else in the world. Most people, mages included, <i>aren't</i> constantly in danger (at least no more so than most people are anyways). Not to say that they're <i>never</i> in danger, but the probability is generally low enough that, like people in real life, they don't need to be constantly on guard and geared out the teeth.</div> </div> </div> </div>We see the setting rather differently then. Think of that: roughly every third mage in the world is your enemy (1/3 Diamond mages, 1/3 Free Council, 1/3 Seers, small fraction of all others), and is going to kill or enslave you if he sees the chance to do it - or will seek to create such chance if he can. Your own friends and colleagues aren't to be trusted, either - they could be Nephandi or Mad. Reaper Legacies like Tremere and Timori don't just survive - Tremere is almost a Nameless Order. There is a lot whole lot of threats. And those aren't just passive threats - they actively seek communities of mages to destroy or subvert or enslave them. And all this is just about other mages - not a word about other Mysteries, which can be just as dangerous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065928#post1065928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind how few mages there actually are in the setting. You're more likely to run into a Sleeper serial killer or the like than you are a Banisher, Scelesti or whatever assuming you aren't knowingly putting yourself out there for them to really notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sleeper serial killer don't actively seek other mages like you. And he isn't much of the threat for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065934#post1065934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Holy shit!</i> What the fuck did you do to get all of them after you at the same time!?</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that obvious? <b><i>You have Awakened</i></b>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T14:25:30-07:00","id":1065941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065935#post1065935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We see the setting rather differently then. Think of that: roughly every third mage in the world is your enemy (1/3 Diamond mages, 1/3 Free Council, 1/3 Seers, small fraction of all others), and is going to kill or enslave you if he sees the chance to do it - or will seek to create such chance if he can. Your own friends and colleagues aren't to be trusted, either - they could be Nephandi or Mad. Reaper Legacies like Tremere and Timori don't just survive - Tremere is almost a Nameless Order. There is a lot whole lot of threats. And those aren't just passive threats - they actively seek communities of mages to destroy or subvert or enslave them. And all this is just about other mages - not a word about other Mysteries, which can be just as dangerous.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sleeper serial killer don't actively seek other mages like you. And he isn't much of the threat for you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Isn't that obvious? <b><i>You have Awakened</i></b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, the Diamond as a whole is bigger than both the Seers and Free Council (individually), and you aren't even including all of the Nameless Orders who aren't nuts. And Seers also aren't that black and white. There's no general kill on sight order going either way as far as I know. The Pentacle and Seers oppose each other, but oppose doesn't necessarily mean kill. I'd assume most Seers aren't going to kill anyone unless specifically ordered to. They're the 'bad guys', but they aren't all individually bloodthirsty kill you in a heartbeat just because levels of evil.<br /> <br /> Also, most Reapers, Scelesti, etc. probably try to actively avoid targeting other mages. Killing mages is more likely to get other mages to investigate them and potentially get them caught. They're much more likely to keep to themselves and target Sleepers. Most of the things you've named are only dangerous to you personally if you are actively snooping around in their business, and are otherwise trying to remain undetected.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T14:41:01-07:00","id":1065945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065941#post1065941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, the Diamond as a whole is bigger than both the Seers and Free Council (individually), and you aren't even including all of the Nameless Orders who aren't nuts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as I recall from the Seers of the Throne, there is two times more mages in Pentacle than in Seers. As the Nameless Orders - I thought they mostly became Free Council and now they more thing of the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065941#post1065941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Seers also aren't that black and white.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book on them won't agree with you, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065941#post1065941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no general kill on sight order going either way as far as I know. They're the 'bad guys', but they aren't all individually bloodthirsty kill you in a heartbeat just because levels of evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they won't kill you at sight, that's because there are worse things than to kill, and some of them can't be done on sight. But they will be done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065941#post1065941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, most Reapers, Scelesti, etc. probably try to actively avoid targeting other mages. </div> </div> </div> </div>Most likely not. Awakened soul is much more powerful than Sleeper one; you can subsist on that one for a longer time. And if mages are careless and aren't prepared, like you suggest, then they are good targets. You may also don't have a choice, like Timori.<br /> There is also Banishers, who are entirely about finding and killing other mages. Most of them die, yes, but they can take other mages with them. They also never die completely and always appear again. In my books, that means that every Consilium potentially can be target of terrorist attack, at any time. <br /> Scelesti may or may not target the mages. But the Abyssal incursions are always threat to the mages, because they try to stop them - no one else can. And Scelesti are never far behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T14:42:10-07:00","id":1065946,"title":"","content":"Scelesti aren't really a threat to Mages directly. They seek Mystery in the Abyss, not to kill or enslave all the other Mages (Typically).<br /> <br /> Seers are only a direct threat to a Mage that gets in their way, most of the time. Mostly because they're outnumbered. The Pentacle has enough infighting to keep them from wiping the Seers (Who also have Supernal beings of immense power backing them up) out so typically they're only a direct threat when you get in their wa as well.<br /> <br /> Does it boil over into open conflict? Frequently! It's still not enough to justify such total paranoia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-21-2017, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T14:50:04-07:00","id":1065950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065946#post1065946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still not enough to justify such total paranoia.</div> </div> </div> </div>If wearing some Shielding spell 24/7 is paranoia for you, then you just have no idea about what total paranoia is, that's all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T14:56:53-07:00","id":1065960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065945#post1065945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as I recall from the Seers of the Throne, there is two times more mages in Pentacle than in Seers. As the Nameless Orders - I thought they mostly became Free Council and now they more thing of the past.<br /> <br /> <br /> The book on them won't agree with you, no.<br /> <br /> <br /> If they won't kill you at sight, that's because there are worse things than to kill, and some of them can't be done on sight. But they will be done.<br /> <br /> <br /> Most likely not. Awakened soul is much more powerful than Sleeper one; you can subsist on that one for a longer time. And if mages are careless and aren't prepared, like you suggest, then they are good targets. You may also don't have a choice, like Timori.<br /> There is also Banishers, who are entirely about finding and killing other mages. Most of them die, yes, but they can take other mages with them. They also never die completely and always appear again. In my books, that means that every Consilium potentially can be target of terrorist attack, at any time.<br /> Scelesti may or may not target the mages. But the Abyssal incursions are always threat to the mages, because they try to stop them - no one else can. And Scelesti are never far behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some became Free Council, but there's still a lot that just don't wanna deal with Awakened politics so they stay out of it.<br /> <br /> Except it doesn't. They're bad guys, definitely, but they aren't all mindless killers. They're typically a darker shade of gray, and they generally do bad things, but especially at the lower ranks (which contain the most people) they're much closer to your average person than they are murderers.<br /> <br /> Awakened Souls are much more dangerous to get a hold of and takes Mastery to take. So unless you're trying to tell me that all Reapers are Masters of Death, I think you're <i>really</i> overestimating how much they tend to go after other mages just for their souls.<br /> <br /> And Banishers are a thing but they're generally under trained and reckless, so they get caught and killed extremely quickly 90% of the time. And dangerous Abyssal Intrusions aren't <i>that</i> common, and when it happens, it's often obvious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065950#post1065950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If wearing some Shielding spell 24/7 is paranoia for you, then you just have no idea about what total paranoia is, that's all.</div> </div> </div> </div>We aren't talking about just 1 or 2 shielding spells here. We're talking about the whole kit and caboodle here. Like 5-6+. That's paranoia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-21-2017, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:05:04-07:00","id":1065967,"title":"","content":"On the topic of Seers, I got the feeling that they and the Pentacle weren't at open war in 2E. (Don't know about 1E.) There's a few mentions of fighting between them in the core book, but it also mentions that Seers are able to have civil enough relations with the Pentacle in order to recruit out of their enemies' ranks. That's impossible if the general attitude is &quot;kill on sight&quot; (or worse). And reading this forum has given me the impression that the Pentacle and Seers can even cooperate if they face common threats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:08:31-07:00","id":1065968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065967#post1065967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of Seers, I got the feeling that they and the Pentacle weren't at open war in 2E. (Don't know about 1E.) There's a few mentions of fighting between them in the core book, but it also mentions that Seers are able to have civil enough relations with the Pentacle in order to recruit out of their enemies' ranks. That's impossible if the general attitude is &quot;kill on sight&quot; (or worse). And reading this forum has given me the impression that the Pentacle and Seers can even cooperate if they face common threats.</div> </div> </div> </div>They weren't constantly at open war even in 1e IIRC. There were <i>some</i> regions that were I think, but that wasn't the standard. Pentacle Seer relationship is more based off of sabotage, undercutting, student poaching, resource stealing, and things of that nature. Closer to highly competitive business competition than two nations at war. It could spark skirmishes and hostilities, sure, but it wasn't assumed to be a constant thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:20:37-07:00","id":1065975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065960#post1065960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it doesn't. They're bad guys, definitely, but they aren't all mindless killers. They're typically a darker shade of gray, and they generally do bad things, but especially at the lower ranks (which contain the most people) they're much closer to your average person than they are murderers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still won't make them any less bad. They may not kill you from the get go. But they will find you, make your life living hell and then make offer you can't refuse. Or they may just kill you again. Nothing personal, only religion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065960#post1065960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awakened Souls are much more dangerous to get a hold of and takes Mastery to take. So unless you're trying to tell me that all Reapers are Masters of Death, I think you're <i>really</i> overestimating how much they tend to go after other mages just for their souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if they are rare, the need to have a steady flow of Awakened souls mean that they will attack again and again. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065960#post1065960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Banishers are a thing but they're generally under trained and reckless, so they get caught and killed extremely quickly 90% of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The remaining 10% is more than enough for any sane mage to wear Shielding spell and have some amulets for surprise attack. I am not even talking about Sanctums, which will be a magic fortresses under such condition, each and every of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065960#post1065960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We aren't talking about just 1 or 2 shielding spells here. We're talking about the whole kit and caboodle here. Like 5-6+. That's paranoia.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are going to be attacked - no, it's not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:20:54-07:00","id":1065977,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but that 5-6 spells is just practicality of having a Cabal. The difference between shielding just yourself and shielding your whole Cabal is a single Reach. And Shielding Spells with longer Durations become better than shorter spells, so when your life is at stake, it's better to have a year long XYZ Shield than to be &quot;fuck, too bad Josephine is not here, I really could use a Mind Shield right now&quot;. Hell, I could see such a Spell Aegis being something to be proud of, like gang colors or uniform; &quot;Look at how cool is our Cabals Aegis, it's super amazing, I'm so proud of being a part of such great group&quot; etc. <br /> As for Peripheral Sight...assuming they trigger it [again, it's trivial to get your stuff Veiled], the same reasoning goes for quality of life stuff like &quot;I have universal translator 24/24&quot;, &quot;I'm always connected to the Internet because LOL INTERNET BRAIN&quot;, &quot;Magic finally allows me to match my body to my true self&quot;, &quot;I'm a Prime Wizard and I've cast As Above As Below on my Shadow Name because ITS SWEEEEEEEET DEAL&quot;, &quot;Hi I'm Acanthus I love being always lucky&quot;, and &quot;I'm edgy teenager who literally wears clothes made from shadows&quot;. I honestly can't see Mages abandoning their ability to enhance their everyday life and define themselves using their long term magic simply because &quot;someone might not like the fact that I have a lot of spells on me&quot;. <br /> And a lot of these spells might be even Indefinite and Safely Relinquished. Do you expect mages to dispel their gender transformation spell they literally invested a Willpower dot into just because &quot;it triggers someone's Peripheral Sight and that might mean they have superkill hung spell on them&quot; when they go for 23 minutes to their Order's hangout to drop a monthly paper on their research? <br /> By the way, if Peripheral Sight reacts to spells when they just linger [instead of them actively doing something], then man, being in a building with more than 3 mages must make you hate your Peripheral Sight. DINGDINGDINGDINGDINGDINGDINGDINGDINGDIGNDIGNDIGNDI GNIDGNIDNGIDNGIDGNDIGNIDGNIDNGIDGNIDNGIDGNDIGND. I guess it could be common etiquette for places like that to Veil your stuff before entering so people won't have a equivalent of Messenger tingle hammering their symbolic brains every two seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:24:43-07:00","id":1065979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065968#post1065968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They weren't constantly at open war even in 1e IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's take a look back, shall we?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Hegemonic Ministry wants to enslave the Pentacle. Visionaries see a day when Pentacle mages pay the Throne a tribute in Mana and lore. They\u2019re Thralls in this future; they only cast spells to serve their masters. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Panopticon\u2019s mages aren\u2019t interested in Thralls or converts. The Ministry\u2019s philosophy is a pragmatic, absolute dictum: kill them all. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ministry of Paternoster wants Pentacle mages to convert or die. Hierodules don\u2019t act out their wishes in wild killing sprees, of course. Holy war is a calculated, organized activity predicated on practical as well as spiritual benefits. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Praetorian Ministry wants an eternal enemy: a hunted, desperate underclass in the Exarchs\u2019 dominion. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:27:56-07:00","id":1065981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065977#post1065977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, if Peripheral Sight reacts to spells when they just linger</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. Not by default.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:40:28-07:00","id":1065992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065981#post1065981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't. Not by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's not a Veiling spell it does because it's an active supernatural effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:40:58-07:00","id":1065995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065918#post1065918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Average sleeper isn't hunted by Seers, Banishers, Tremere, other Reapers, Scelesti, hunters and everyone else at once.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>All </i>mages in danger <i>all </i>the time. That goes with being a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seers does not hunt you. Most of them want to recruit you.<br /> Tremere, Lichs and Reapers are really rare, and Tremeres have a highly organized society that makes very hard to know the extension of their influence and power.<br /> Banishers and Scelesti are the real problems here. But hey, thank god they also rare.<br /> <br /> Awakening is a rare ocasion, and those enemies are all awakened, I would be more cautious about not being shot in a crime than being outright murdered by a Scelesti.<br /> <br /> Again, living on a violent country, I do not walk around carrying a gun everywhere, cause that can attract attention, even for my own protection. I do feel safe when I'm at my work, inside an office and at my home, cause I assume these are places where someone will not try to kill me.<br /> <br /> If I can throw mind controlling devices and stuff like that here, I would also feel safe at work. It seems to stupid to use mind control on someone at an office to kill another person, it raises to many questions and attention. Society provide a feeling of safeness/security. Even on tales about monsters, a monster is terrifying for a single victim, but a violent mob is terrifying for the monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:44:55-07:00","id":1065998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065975#post1065975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are going to be attacked - no, it's not.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record I actually think that it's probably not that big a deal to most Awakened to run into others or be themselves under the protection of a lot of spells defensive or otherwise. I do think you're greatly exaggerating the threat level most Mages feel like they're under though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:47:14-07:00","id":1066000,"title":"","content":"Now, player characters on the other hand. But they always live more intensive and dangerous lives than their peers because otherwise it's difficult to tell interesting stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:47:54-07:00","id":1066001,"title":"","content":"I might have fake memories, but wasn't there a really big conversation about Peripheral Mage Sight shortly after the book came out and the consensus at the end of it was something like &quot;spell to make a sword ablaze when moonlight shines upon it doesn't trigger peripheral sight, until it actively does stuff when moonlight shines upon the sword&quot;, where basically spell has to be actively doing something to be considered active, like when Ghost needs to do Ghostly stuff to trigger peripheral sight? <br /> I don't even know how to search for that topic, so maybe someone with better search fu could embark upon a archive dive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:49:38-07:00","id":1066003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065995#post1065995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seers does not hunt you. Most of them want to recruit you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correction: they want to enslave you. At best. At worst, you are really much better dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065995#post1065995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tremere, Lichs and Reapers are really rare, and Tremeres have a highly organized society that makes very hard to know the extension of their influence and power.<br /> Banishers and Scelesti are the real problems here. But hey, thank god they also rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many rare enemies together aren't so rare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065995#post1065995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awakening is a rare ocasion, and those enemies are all awakened, I would be more cautious about not being shot in a crime than being outright murdered by a Scelesti.</div> </div> </div> </div>One more reason to wear Shielding spells every day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065995#post1065995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Society provide a feeling of safeness/security. Even on tales about monsters, a monster is terrifying for a single victim, but a violent mob is terrifying for the monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's just that - a feeling. In this very thread there were a plenty of example on how mages can make tracking murder back extremely hard. Violent mob isn't terrifying, if it have no enemy to strike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:51:37-07:00","id":1066006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1066001#post1066001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might have fake memories, but wasn't there a really big conversation about Peripheral Mage Sight shortly after the book came out and the consensus at the end of it was something like &quot;spell to make a sword ablaze when moonlight shines upon it doesn't trigger peripheral sight, until it actively does stuff when moonlight shines upon the sword&quot;, where basically spell has to be actively doing something to be considered active, like when Ghost needs to do Ghostly stuff to trigger peripheral sight?<br /> I don't even know how to search for that topic, so maybe someone with better search fu could embark upon a archive dive?</div> </div> </div> </div>That specific effect on the sword would have to be a hung spell with a conditional duration, the spell that does the hanging would ping PMS, but the spell that's hanging wouldn't since it effectively doesn't exist at the moment.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, it could be a spell imbued into an item or an artifact but in those cases the spell doesn't actually exist until the conditions for it being cast are met.<br /> <br /> Basically though, a spell doesn't have a &quot;neutral&quot; existence state wherein it's not actively doing something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-21-2017, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:55:19-07:00","id":1066008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065992#post1065992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's not a Veiling spell it does because it's an active supernatural effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. Shields and alike are passive effects. Examples given in Peripheral Mage Sight clearly give that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065998#post1065998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think you're greatly exaggerating the threat level most Mages feel like they're under though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just how I see and GM the Mage games. I see them are mystical gnostic stories of horror and paranoia. Given that there is no &quot;canonical&quot; level of threats in CofD, we are arguing about tastes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:57:41-07:00","id":1066010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1066008#post1066008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it isn't. Shields and alike are passive effects. Examples given in Peripheral Mage Sight clearly give that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to have to cite that because I just reread the PMS section and only concealment powers go under the radar for PMS from what I'm seeing. A Shielding spell isn't passive, it's actively protecting you from something even if the thing it's protecting you from isn't present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:03:31-07:00","id":1066013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1066010#post1066010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Shielding spell isn't passive, it's actively protecting you from something even if the thing it's protecting you from isn't present.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is passive - it &quot;works&quot; only when protecting someone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Peripheral Mage Sight, for instance, doesn\u2019t detect a ghost lurking quietly in Twilight. If the ghost <b>spends </b>Essence, <b>activates</b> a Numen, or <b>Manifests</b>, however, this attracts the mage\u2019s attention. </div> </div> </div>I read it so that PMS &quot;pings&quot; only then somebody <b>casts </b>the spell, not when there is active magic around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:09:06-07:00","id":1066017,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, different interpretation. I don't let a spell's presence just drop off the radar after it's been cast because I figure a Mage must spend some amount of his energy on maintaining it at all times. Spending a WP point or dot doesn't mitigate that either because the Mage has simply divorced the energy for maintaining the spell from his person but it's still there.<br /> <br /> The equivalent to the ghost in Twilight not triggering PMS for Mages is a Mage who isn't using or maintaining any spells the way I read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:13:34-07:00","id":1066020,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't remember the answer that was reached in the original topic about this. I know I went with the interpretation similar to Dark Archons, mostly because it made investigating Mysteries more exciting, allowing certain spells and effects to hide in plain sight until you poke them right way and they go &quot;ping&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:19:12-07:00","id":1066023,"title":"","content":"I think this is the exact reason we have three types of mage sight, and it doesn't seem to me to fall under passive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:20:00-07:00","id":1066024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065975#post1065975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still won't make them any less bad. They may not kill you from the get go. But they will find you, make your life living hell and then make offer you can't refuse. Or they may just kill you again. Nothing personal, only religion.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even if they are rare, the need to have a steady flow of Awakened souls mean that they will attack again and again.<br /> <br /> <br /> The remaining 10% is more than enough for any sane mage to wear Shielding spell and have some amulets for surprise attack. I am not even talking about Sanctums, which will be a magic fortresses under such condition, each and every of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you are going to be attacked - no, it's not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It kinda does. Not being a mass murderer typically means you're not as bad of a person than if you were. Just in general.<br /> <br /> Again, it's a matter of probability, just like you said. There aren't that many of them and even fewer are going to be Masters. They exist, but you aren't going to need to live your life in anticipation of such a meeting.<br /> <br /> And not really. Just like there are probably a small subset of serial killers or terrorists that are smart enough to get away with it, normal people don't live their lives in a state of constant preparation. Some people get a bit crazy with it, but it generally isn't that much of a concern for most.<br /> <br /> IF. You don't seem to understand that there's a big IF in this equation. Most people don't expect to be killed at any moment. Most mages don't expect to be killed at any moment, and they live like that was the case. And any deviation to that is going to be considered strange to them and <i>will</i> have social consequences, even if it is something like lower First Impression, penalties to social rolls, denied entrance into their territory while armed up, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1066001#post1066001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might have fake memories, but wasn't there a really big conversation about Peripheral Mage Sight shortly after the book came out and the consensus at the end of it was something like &quot;spell to make a sword ablaze when moonlight shines upon it doesn't trigger peripheral sight, until it actively does stuff when moonlight shines upon the sword&quot;, where basically spell has to be actively doing something to be considered active, like when Ghost needs to do Ghostly stuff to trigger peripheral sight?<br /> I don't even know how to search for that topic, so maybe someone with better search fu could embark upon a archive dive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, as far as I know, as long as a spell is active, and by that I mean exists really, it pings PMS unless veiling or being veiled. Shields are actively defending you throughout their entire duration. For example, a Mental Shield is <i>always</i> blocking all mind affecting abilities, even when there are no mind affecting abilities bashing against it at that very moment. It doesn't turn off and turn back on only when needed, the effect is constant. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-21-2017, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:21:48-07:00","id":1066026,"title":"","content":"Again on why the other mages aren't really that scary all the time:<br /> <br /> Most Seers battle each other for position.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Advancement comes when a Seer is strong enough to demand it \u2014 most Seers watch their superiors for weakness while working to undermine their inferiors. </div> </div> </div>Also, on Duel Arcane, there are examples of Seers dueling against Pentacle to solve differences or problems.<br /> <br /> The Mad Ones are not always dangerous. Or at least they are not dangerous all the time.<br /> <br /> The Banishers are not only rare, but some of them also commit suicide. Also:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some mages take it upon themselves to kill those Banishers resulting from a twisted Awakening, seeing it as an act of kindness \u2014 better to end their pain now than drive them to further pain and madness. </div> </div> </div>That seems to be a thing for the Arrows or the Guardians.<br /> <br /> Liches are not only rare, but come in such different ways that they are really more of a Mysteries than an active threath. They can be just echoes(ghost liches), or entirely different things. It is a point of view, but there is much more advantages on kidnapping a Mage than outright killing it, wich is a great material for a plot.<br /> <br /> Not every Reaper will try to steal a Mage Soul. Some are described as drug dealers on the book.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A few become pushers, dealing souls to more squeamish mages who desire the rush of power but do not want to harvest the soul themselves. The first hit\u2019s free, but after a time, anyone who feels the benefits of becoming a Reaper will find her own supply. </div> </div> </div>People already talked about the Scelesti and the Abyss exploration, so I'll let that out of this post.<br /> <br /> Again, thats just my opinion, but you are making it look like every one of the mage enemies are outright murders. I feel like you're trying to express that every drug dealer is a murder, every burglar will stab you (always), every paranoid person will shoot you on sight and things like that. And that's not true. These people need to bolster their numbers, they need supplies, money, mana, etc. They all live on the same world as the characters live, they all have their own obssessions. Killing is not the only, nor the best, way to deal with things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T17:00:09-07:00","id":1066046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065995#post1065995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even on tales about monsters, a monster is terrifying for a single victim, but a violent mob is terrifying for the monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>This<br /> This is something I believe gets overlooked a lot. The power of numbers can overwhelm a lot of things. and it's modeled in the system. What makes Hunters work in setting is the cell. 4-5 people working together amplifying their strengths and minimizing their weaknesses. Its why the masqeruade is a thing. A unified and focused effort of even a small town can overthrow a vampire lord.<br /> <br /> And thats why I like it. getting enough people on your side can swing the advantage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T17:25:05-07:00","id":1066058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065935#post1065935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that obvious? <b><i>You have Awakened</i></b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that like it makes the mage is worth attention for that alone.<br /> <br /> They aren't. They're just fish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T17:34:43-07:00","id":1066062,"title":"","content":"Fish who tend to think that they are super important, on verge of unveiling secrets of eternity, and who just discovered a whole array of getting what they want, and what's even worse, understanding that there is plenty of people who can do these things too, probably are doing them, and maybe even have done them to you and you didn't even know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T18:11:40-07:00","id":1066075,"title":"","content":"Stepping into the faulty memory arena, I remember there being the exact opposite conversation, where Dave stepped in and said that a Ward or a Ban just sitting there and not blocking anything still makes your crazy wizard bullshit radar go ping. I went checking the archives, though, and cannot find anything on it for the life of me.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, Mages are rare and capable of massive reprisals that make them killing one another - even sworn enemies like the Pentacle and Seers - rare and important events. PCs being PCs will see such events more often than most Mages ever will, but the background rate is probably a bit like being a member of the mob; people getting whacked happens enough to just be a fact of life, but not often enough that you don't still go out each night.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T06:59:40-07:00","id":1066282,"title":"","content":"Maybe my examples of safety steps might have been not the best analogies to what a mage can do.<br /> <br /> How often do people always take the time to stop and listen to the weather report before going about their normal day, not talking about planned special outings, just their daily routine?<br /> <br /> How many people <u>always</u> check the traffic report before starting their commute?<br /> <br /> How many people <u>always</u> carry one of those little packages of kleenex's or hand sanitizer?<br /> <br /> How many people <u>always</u> keep an umbrella, just in case?<br /> <br /> How many people <u>always</u> carry a taser, pepper spray, or a handgun for protect?<br /> <br /> If they don't check the weather weather or traffic reports they can't know what to expect, thus ruining their ability to gauge probability accurately. Weather and traffic are things in constant flux and affect our lives.<br /> <br /> If the above is uncommon, and some are even rare, doesn't that add credibility that people are affected by akrasia, and 'mages' being just a subset of 'people' are no more immune to it than others? Most people do not run a conscious risk assessment matrix in their lives, which explains their complacent action and the high degree of accidents and tragedies in real life, and the world of darkness where people, mages included, are oppressed by the Lie it'd seem to me that akrasia would be more pronounced not less. How else do you explain all the people choosing the wrong choices when they know better?<br /> <br /> Also with heart disease being the #1 killer, explain bacon and cigarettes if people always avoid the most probable causes of death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-22-2017, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T07:56:33-07:00","id":1066305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1066282#post1066282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they don't check the weather weather or traffic reports they can't know what to expect, thus ruining their ability to gauge probability accurately</div> </div> </div> </div>Even then, human brains are <i>garbage</i> at probability. Cognitive bias, selection bias, inability to imagine circumstances different from the ones you're used to, inability to imagine one's own failure, etc.<br /> <br /> A Mage brought up as a sheltered rich kid in the sub-urbs will view the world as being much safer than a gang member on the poor side of New York.<br /> <br /> Even in construction and engineering, where people are <i>trained</i> in workplace safety and security, we see this all the time (true stories):<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh I'll just walk up this plank without a harness, I've got good balance nothing bad's gonna happen&quot;<br /> *loses balance, breaks his back*<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh I'll just oil this industrial grain dispenser from the inside, it's off so nothing bad can happen&quot;<br /> *oil releases built up torque from friction, grain dispenser decapitates guy*<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh I'll just bypass this safety switch which requires both hands to activate by duct-taping one of the buttons, I'll work more efficiently that way&quot;<br /> *gets entire arm crushed by machine*<br /> <br /> These people weren't any more or less &quot;stupid&quot; than any other human being. Brains are just garbage at predicting things they've never experienced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:57:51-07:00","id":1066343,"title":"","content":"Something worth considering in this is that trauma affects people's behaviours. The brain compensates for exposure to traumatic situations by trying to assess ways in which to prevent that trauma in future and can, if the behaviour becomes maladaptive, lead to pathologies. <br /> <br /> That sort of response can be healthy if the person works through it properly and comes to a more realistic perspective. Taking more care to be observant when driving, for example, is a healthy reaction to a car crash. Refusing to near a vehicle is not.<br /> <br /> Mages, of course, are obsessive loons whose pursuit of dangerous experiences is not only hard for a human mind to process, are not only fundamentally isolated from the majority of humanity (and thus from opportunities to process and contextualize trauma), but also exist among peers who have a worrying tendency to confuse madness with insight and encourage delusions.<br /> <br /> The list of threats that exist to Mages are as infinite as they are to the rest of humanity, with the added benefit of self-imposed danger on top of it. If a Mage has trouble adapting to traumatic experiences, they will develop maladaptive focuses on specific threats that they ward against to extremes. I've got a story in my pocket involving my Thyrsus refusing to even touch magical objects and suffering a stress breakdown in their presence because her first experience was so awful.<br /> <br /> No Mage is prepared for everything, but those who do fall into paranoia will fall hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}